{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition","id":1310339,"title":"Metis' role in the 5th edition?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-05-06T12:11:10-07:00","id":1310339,"title":"Metis' role in the 5th edition?","content":"So let us say that you get to decide some aspect of the (to be) 5th edition, mainly the breeds. You still want homid and lupus to be there, but what about metis?<br /> <br /> Here I move to the meat of this thread. If WtA faces the kind of heavy restructuring that Vampire went under, should the metis breed still remain in the game?<br /> <br /> For one, what message does it send to the players that the garouxgarou child is a deformed and infertile creature, named rather poorly as metis? This isn't 90s anymore, we are more aware of players who are disabled. Or what about the actual Canadian metis people?<br /> <br /> Then there is the fact that metis have zero actual werewolf myth role. They are very much a combination of <a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/TheGrotesque\" target=\"_blank\">The Grotesque</a> and <a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/MadwomanInTheAttic\" target=\"_blank\">Madwoman in the Attic </a>tropes. Not as much on anything werewolf myths have.<br /> <br /> Then again, metis serve as a good example of garou pride and arrogance, not to mention moral blindness. They are very much the example how dark garou society can be at times.<br /> <br /> What do you guys think?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-06T12:54:04-07:00","id":1310351,"title":"","content":"Metis are a part of Werewolf, I would say they should be kept as such. They don\u2019t have to obviously and can make a different choice since they are the content creators. <br /> <br /> Just because people deal with deformities in the real world does not mean that we should remove them in fiction. How they are portrayed is another discussion and they can be portrayed as a capable part of the society as those with deformities are in the real world. As far as naming If they change it they change it, doesn\u2019t really matter to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe","name":"Redwulfe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-06T13:25:24-07:00","id":1310359,"title":"","content":"I don't think you can call something W5 and just white-wash over the Metis existing in the game and cut them. To keep it a WtA game, and not a new Werewolf game (Forsaken already cut them out for instance), I would do the best I could to address issues with them rather than just axing them.<br /> <br /> Work on the name? Yes, though it's a bit harder than it sounds unless you redo the whole language of the game. One of my choices here would be to keep it Metis, but explicitly make it clear that the Garou are referring to the Greek goddess Metis (which has a lot of resonance that's less dismissive/diminishing of people with disabilities and plays more with sins of pride and prophecies of future doom), not the French metis for mixed race individuals. I'd also include a sidebar acknowledging it as an OOC saving throw rather than insult anyone's intelligence by trying to pretend it was always meant to be that way.<br /> <br /> This is also a way to adjust the fiction around the Metis. I would do things like introduce the idea that the first Metis were not cursed with deformities or infertility. As Zeus feared losing his status to his child with Metis, the Garou feared the Metis would usurp all of the power in the Nation despite Gaia saying the Garou weren't supposed to do make Metis (or did she?). It is then the Garou - as Zeus sinned by eating Metis - who somehow messed things up. Also it's the Garou... messing everything up is what they do. They plead for the spirits to enforce the Litany, and, thus their persecution of the Metis is that much more hypocritical. This also plays well off the other Fera who generally don't have Metis issues (either they can't make kids that way, or no problems occur).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-07T04:40:28-07:00","id":1310511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1310359#post1310359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think you can call something W5 and just white-wash over the Metis existing in the game and cut them. To keep it a WtA game, and not a new Werewolf game (Forsaken already cut them out for instance), I would do the best I could to address issues with them rather than just axing them.<br /> <br /> Work on the name? Yes, though it's a bit harder than it sounds unless you redo the whole language of the game. One of my choices here would be to keep it Metis, but explicitly make it clear that the Garou are referring to the Greek goddess Metis (which has a lot of resonance that's less dismissive/diminishing of people with disabilities and plays more with sins of pride and prophecies of future doom), not the French metis for mixed race individuals. I'd also include a sidebar acknowledging it as an OOC saving throw rather than insult anyone's intelligence by trying to pretend it was always meant to be that way.<br /> <br /> This is also a way to adjust the fiction around the Metis. I would do things like introduce the idea that the first Metis were not cursed with deformities or infertility. As Zeus feared losing his status to his child with Metis, the Garou feared the Metis would usurp all of the power in the Nation despite Gaia saying the Garou weren't supposed to do make Metis (or did she?). It is then the Garou - as Zeus sinned by eating Metis - who somehow messed things up. Also it's the Garou... messing everything up is what they do. They plead for the spirits to enforce the Litany, and, thus their persecution of the Metis is that much more hypocritical. This also plays well off the other Fera who generally don't have Metis issues (either they can't make kids that way, or no problems occur).</div> </div> </div> </div>Just a note, <b>I'm</b> <b>not</b> saying metis should be taken out. Basically just thinking on what a writer would change if they were going for different take on werewolves in the setting.<br /> <br /> What about them is werewolf rather than another trope? In Forsaken, as cool as the unihar were, the uratha never really NEEDED metis the same way as garou do.<br /> <br /> I'd change the name to something like Pravus (bad/misshapen in latin) to imply how they can be seen. I'd also maybe take away more 'human' deformities, to imply that what is wrong with metis isn't due to them being disabled/infertile but a spiritual fuck up. Plus, garou can still be born with regular disabilities so metis ones being clearly different would add to the distance between the breeds.<br /> <br /> The tribal treatments are fine, as they were VERY well explored over the years.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-07T05:51:00-07:00","id":1310516,"title":"","content":"Short: I'd keep Metis as Metis.<br /> <br /> Long: In the WW lore the Metis has a place &amp; a purpose. Their existence is a failsafe. They remind the People that they are dependent on their Kin &amp; on humanity With the Metis (as a punishment) their relationship is co-existence (in theory) as protector &amp; mate.<br /> <br /> Without them it would be reasonable to breed just in themeselves (Curse, Veil, function, camaradice, etc.). This could and would have destroyed humanity long ago or fallen to the Wyrm in hubris.<br /> <br /> Yeh it's not 90's, but is it really neccesary to modify a games spirit to make it politicaly correct? Do we really have to cut out critical parts? How many metis people felt abused by the WW game?<br /> <br /> I say, keep the soul of this RPG or if it wouldn't be profitable, create a new one. For me it's always pain to find my old RPGs mangled to fit the zeitgeist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/562-lachdanan","name":"Lachdanan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-07T05:57:40-07:00","id":1310518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lachdanan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1310516#post1310516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Short: I'd keep Metis as Metis.<br /> <br /> Long: In the WW lore the Metis has a place &amp; a purpose. Their existence is a failsafe. They remind the People that they are dependent on their Kin &amp; on humanity With the Metis (as a punishment) their relationship is co-existence (in theory) as protector &amp; mate.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it is politically correct to reconsider metis' role as 'punishment', as many players of WoD are disabled themselves (one of them, yo.) Or that the abuse they face is 'justified' if even a little. Heavy Arms above offered a good alternative way to justify the metis without implying disability is a punishment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-07T06:12:31-07:00","id":1310522,"title":"","content":"I think one of the reasons Metis existed in the first place was to answer the question, if we have werewolves who are born from humans (homids) and werewolves who are born from wolves (lupus), then what happens when it is the werewolves who mate? If you remove the Metis breed, you still have that question to answer.<br /> <br /> Now it is true that Metis don't exist as actual werewolf myth and folklore. But MOST of the game is like that. In folklore, werewolves are simply humans practicing black magic to turn into wolves which then attacks and kill livestock or their fellow man. There is no lupus breed. There is no crinos form (or glabro or hispo). There are no auspices or tribes. There is no connection to the moon. Some of these accrued to the myth due to modern movies and books which developed the basic concept in its own way, but they aren't any more (or less) authentic than new WtA concepts.<br /> <br /> I am fine with Metis as is. I believe an aspect of the Changing Breeds is that Gaia wanted them to serve as a bridge between the two worlds (man's and nature/animal). So homids learned what it meant to be animal, and lupus learned what it meant to be human. They're supposed to take that back to their people. However, when Garou breed with Garou, that doesn't happen. Instead of becoming a bridge between two worlds, they're stuck in their own world as their parents (and society) are neither human nor animal.. That isn't what Gaia wanted, so that is why Garou are not supposed to breed with each other. For breaking the taboo, their children are marked. To me, this works on a thematic level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-07T08:57:08-07:00","id":1310544,"title":"","content":"I think we should keep Metis<br /> <br /> but I think Breed Auspice, and Tribe should no longer influence starting Traits.<br /> <br /> give other bonuses to make up for not starting with higher Gnosis.<br /> <br /> Like in Changeling 20","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-07T10:40:41-07:00","id":1310572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1310511#post1310511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd change the name to something like Pravus (bad/misshapen in latin) to imply how they can be seen. I'd also maybe take away more 'human' deformities, to imply that what is wrong with metis isn't due to them being disabled/infertile but a spiritual fuck up.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure any of this gets away from the issues with the Metis besides the name. They're still being punished for their parent's inability to keep it in their pants.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lachdanan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1310516#post1310516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They remind the People that they are dependent on their Kin &amp; on humanity With the Metis (as a punishment) their relationship is co-existence (in theory) as protector &amp; mate.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's completely unnecessary to have the Metis to have this effect though. If every Garou-Garou mating resulted in a horribly painful miscarriage it would have the same enforcement aspect without treating disabled children as a divine punishment on their parents.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Without them it would be reasonable to breed just in themeselves (Curse, Veil, function, camaradice, etc.). This could and would have destroyed humanity long ago or fallen to the Wyrm in hubris. </div> </div> </div>This is basically what happened anyway. The Garou have largely abandoned humanity and just breed in their little family groups of Kinfolk. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yeh it's not 90's, but is it really neccesary to modify a games spirit to make it politicaly correct? </div> </div> </div>People have been talking about this and how to address it since the 90s. I don't care what labels you want to toss on the idea. People have been turned off the game for decades because of the &quot;Metis are punished with disabilities to show their parents a lesson,&quot; thing. it's been demonstrated time and time again that nothing the Metis add to the game can't be done a different (and frankly better) way, and those ways mean more people want to play the game. Why not change it if that's the case?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How many metis people felt abused by the WW game? </div> </div> </div>How does it matter?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1310522#post1310522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think one of the reasons Metis existed in the first place was to answer the question, if we have werewolves who are born from humans (homids) and werewolves who are born from wolves (lupus), then what happens when it is the werewolves who mate? If you remove the Metis breed, you still have that question to answer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, lots of possible ways to do that, but to condense a bitt:<br /> <br /> 1a) Garou-Garou matings don't result in pregnancy. They can bone all they want, try any magics they want, but in the end nothing will work. If the Garou want kids, they have to look outside themselves.<br /> <br /> 1b) As mentioned above, make this any number of degrees harsher with things like the fetus will never survive, or steal the unihar concept from Forsaken for some extra &quot;you done fucked up,&quot; consequences. This is all stuff that makes 1a worse without changing the answer.<br /> <br /> 2) The mating never results directly in more Garou. The offspring are either normal humans or wolves depending on the mother's Breed, or sometimes Kin. You can tack on other things like these offspring don't get Pure Breed or whatever.<br /> <br /> 3) The mating results in a spirit that's pulled off into the Umbra for whatever reasons and for whatever purposes, which can range from good and innocent to horrible. There's no breed to play, and the Garou have little known reasons to accept this is a good thing to do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I am fine with Metis as is. I believe an aspect of the Changing Breeds is that Gaia wanted them to serve as a bridge between the two worlds (man's and nature/animal). </div> </div> </div>I think being fine with the Metis as-is is being fine with some really questionable stuff. I'm comfortable with saying it would be too big of a change to avoid, &quot;this isn't Apocalypse anymore&quot; backlash, but that's not the same thing.<br /> <br /> The &quot;bridge&quot; issue suffers in a lot of places:<br /> <br /> 1) It doesn't actually work, the Garou just select small groups of insular human families to breed with instead.<br /> <br /> 2) It doesn't make sense for the Metis to even be possible. If Gaia truly wants there to be no Garou-Garou mating... why not make it impossible for that to happen? <br /> <br /> 3) This why I suggested some of what I did earlier. If the Metis originally - and according to Gaia's design - weren't being used like this implies, and rather as the bridge between Homids and Lupus to make the whole bridge concept functional, there's a lot more merit towards them having a real place in the intended functioning of Garou society.<br /> <br /> 4) It doesn't really address why so many of the other Fera never have this problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-07T15:07:13-07:00","id":1310623,"title":"","content":"I really like the metis, conceptually. They're really the whole 'child paying for the sins of their parents' thing that personally I find really compelling as a story hook. That said, I also recognize that they can be hella problematic, and 5E would be a good time to hardcore course correct on that. I like the idea that they carry some sort of deformity, but I'd really like to see it be more of a supernatural deformity/limitation than any real-world sort of thing. <br /> <br /> Also, I'm all for changing the breed name. It costs nothing to avoid being offensive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25290-palmedfire","name":"palmedfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25290_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-07T20:45:31-07:00","id":1310665,"title":"","content":"Werewolf is pretty heavily about balancing the Glories of your Elders with holding the SIns of their mistakes. The Metis are perhaps the most blatant but are part and parcel to everything from the Interegum, to the the War of Rage to the Apocalypse itself... Do Metis need to be deformed for them to hold their parents &quot;Sins&quot;? Being Sterile is a pretty big deal by itself..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-07T22:15:15-07:00","id":1310680,"title":"","content":"I think the problem with the Metis as written, is that they don't really sell the &quot;sins of their mistakes&quot; aspect. It's not like a Metis' distant descendant is going to pay some sort of price in all this.. they aren't ever going to exist. That's one of the reasons I like a change to the lore where the Garou Metis weren't originally punished at all, but like all those examples, it's the mistakes of the Garou as a people that drove history in a bad direction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-07T22:50:30-07:00","id":1310687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1310680#post1310680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the problem with the Metis as written, is that they don't really sell the &quot;sins of their mistakes&quot; aspect. It's not like a Metis' distant descendant is going to pay some sort of price in all this.. they aren't ever going to exist. That's one of the reasons I like a change to the lore where the Garou Metis weren't originally punished at all, but like all those examples, it's the mistakes of the Garou as a people that drove history in a bad direction.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Metis are punished for their parents sins. Even the most progressive tribes treat them as second class garou. So while they won't have to deal with descendants, apocalypse at least seems there's a good chance that's true of any breed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-07T23:17:18-07:00","id":1310691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1310518#post1310518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think it is politically correct to reconsider metis' role as 'punishment', as many players of WoD are disabled themselves (one of them, yo.) Or that the abuse they face is 'justified' if even a little. Heavy Arms above offered a good alternative way to justify the metis without implying disability is a punishment.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m sorry to hear about your problem. Really is. We also have two disabled person in our gaming-club and try to fit the game experience to comfort them. (English is my second language, so if I can be equivocal.). I don\u2019t think they are offended by the existence of Metis, and non of us found it more than a role-playing opportunity what can be excluded (a rural wolf-pack with just lupus is an example) if needed.<br /> <br /> It should be empathized that not disabilities are punishment, BUT the (or at least as the Garou see it) existence and disabilities of the Metis.<br /> <br /> About the abuse of the Metis: It\u2019s a different matter. The conservative, dysfunctional patriarchy what is the Garou society punishes/abuses the Metis. It shows the internal problems of their social construct but can be varied from Caern to Caern.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1310572#post1310572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If every Garou-Garou mating resulted in a horribly painful miscarriage it would have the same enforcement aspect without treating disabled children as a divine punishment on their parents.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It\u2019s harder to see your pup have a disability than have a miscarriage. Trust me, I know.<br /> If the existence of metis is really a punishment, it\u2019s a bigger, cruel, heartless, but more efficient one.<br /> BUT we still don\u2019t know if it\u2019s the case. The Garou could attach legends to a problem what affected their life. Back than the existence of Metis was because of too much spirit-stuff contained in the flesh.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1310572#post1310572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is basically what happened anyway. The Garou have largely abandoned humanity and just breed in their little family groups of Kinfolk.</div> </div> </div> </div>More or less, yes, but the chance of peaceful coexistence is still exist.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1310572#post1310572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People have been talking about this and how to address it since the 90s. I don't care what labels you want to toss on the idea. People have been turned off the game for decades because of the &quot;Metis are punished with disabilities to show their parents a lesson,&quot; thing. it's been demonstrated time and time again that nothing the Metis add to the game can't be done a different (and frankly better) way, and those ways mean more people want to play the game. Why not change it if that's the case?</div> </div> </div> </div>Frankly, I *personally* don\u2019t like the Metis. But every game-world is a spider-web. If you start to pull one thread everything moves. That\u2019s my problem with retconning. It messes everything. Metis had a place and role to play. Retcon them is problematic.<br /> Maybe we are too much Eastern-European, but I don\u2019t know anybody who put down WW because of the Metis, but me may be one continent away.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1310572#post1310572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> How does it matter?</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn\u2019t, but was a topic above.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1310572#post1310572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">. If Gaia truly wants there to be no Garou-Garou mating... why not make it impossible for that to happen?</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s what we don\u2019t know.<br /> <br /> By the way, Onyx Path offered us /the writers a tool to change the Metis, namely Shattered Dreams.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/562-lachdanan","name":"Lachdanan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-08T00:38:37-07:00","id":1310698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1310572#post1310572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's completely unnecessary to have the Metis to have this effect though. If every Garou-Garou mating resulted in a horribly painful miscarriage it would have the same enforcement aspect without treating disabled children as a divine punishment on their parents.</div> </div> </div> </div>But then you are punishing the mother for the sexual act, there will be an issue with that if it's the direction they take too.<br /> <br /> The changes to Metis really depend on how you want the issues to be dealt with. <br /> Firstly- the name, it's meant to be pejorative, especially with the ties to Native Americans. Changing it would signify a significant change to attitude to them, A sidebar would make sense if it stays though (Like the old cartoons with disclaimers about racism)<br /> - Sins of the father (or mother too, that counts!) - Is it a problem in general, or just the way it's presented, and what the &quot;Punishments&quot; are?<br /> - Deformities, There has been a bit of a movement to stop tying monstrousness with real-life disabilities. More so in D&amp;D and similar fantasy, but it could be an issue. I've not actually talked to anyone affected personally. Can this be resolved by only having supernatural and not-disability-representing options for the Metis?<br /> <br /> What if the spirits punish the parents of a Metis with marks showing they broke the litany instead of the Metis itself? Gaia declares that the punishment should be on those that transgress instead of the innocent children?<br /> <br /> It'd still give the temptation to create Metis for quickly replenishing their numbers, even though the Metis would be sterile.<br /> <br /> *However, W5 will likely be created with Video games and LARP compatibility in mind (Considering Paradox Interactive) so it may be influenced by BNS Larp versions of what's going on with Metis and the spiritually unawakened werewolves...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","name":"Illithid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16927_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-08T02:19:14-07:00","id":1310702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1310687#post1310687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Metis are punished for their parents sins.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which paints Gaia/etc. as hypocritical assholes rather than highlighting the themes of the next generation trying to clean up the messes of their previous generations without losing pride in the good those that came before them did.<br /> <br /> Most of the things you pointed to are things that happened because the Garou have free will and aren't mindless servants. They're decisions the Garou made, largely collectively, that have had repercussions that then echo throughout history for later generations to have to deal with.<br /> <br /> Metis are unique because they only exist because Gaia either lets them exist, or actively caused them to exist. The majority of Fera either can't make Metis at all, or their Metis have no long term issues beyond the increased difficulty of birthing them. Of the rest, only the Garou and Ratkin have taboos against it, and actually culturally care about enforcing them; the Ajaba like their Metis, and the Bastet are generally ambivalent about it.<br /> <br /> So it's abundantly clear that they don't need to be this way in the setting. It's not some inherent part of the spiritual nature of the changing breeds where this is always the result. There's not reason based on the lore of the game where making a Metis is a sin that's really the Garou's fault instead of Gaia's fault.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...apocalypse at least seems there's a good chance that's true of any breed. </div> </div> </div>This is a W5 thread, and the 5th books are (well as last we heard before big changes happened) not going to continue with the idea that the Time of Judgement signaled a single apocalyptic event, but rather a new era for the World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lachdanan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1310691#post1310691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The conservative, dysfunctional patriarchy what is the Garou society punishes/abuses the Metis.</div> </div> </div> </div>But one that the spirits actively support. There's no spiritual repercussions for being a dick to a Metis like there would be for mistreating other Garou. The Garou might not have to do it, but unless they're serving a small few very specific Totems, there's nothing stopping them from doing it; even as there are mechanisms to punish them for all sorts of other shitty behavior.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It\u2019s harder to see your pup have a disability than have a miscarriage. </div> </div> </div>Does that really matter to the point of punishing the parent who sinned instead of the child that did nothing wrong?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If the existence of metis is really a punishment, it\u2019s a bigger, cruel, heartless, but more efficient one. </div> </div> </div>It doesn't seem terribly efficient to me... as I've detailed earlier. Also the Garou keep making more of them anyway.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> More or less, yes, but the chance of peaceful coexistence is still exist. </div> </div> </div>The chance would probably be better without the spirits enforcing this whole Metis thing, or recognizing Pure Breed as something that matters. The fact that a chance might still exist doesn't really say much about how poorly the Garou were created to maximize that chance instead of minimizing it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But every game-world is a spider-web. If you start to pull one thread everything moves. That\u2019s my problem with retconning. It messes everything. Metis had a place and role to play. Retcon them is problematic. </div> </div> </div>I think you're making perfect the enemy of good here. First, fictional worlds are generally more resilient than you're giving credit, and second retcons are something you can use a new edition to execute to be as minimally disruptive as possible. In the 15+ of metaplot that's going to have happened before the end of WtA Rev. and the start of W5, it's extremely easy to finesse in some retcons along the lines I was mentioning earlier.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Maybe we are too much Eastern-European, but I don\u2019t know anybody who put down WW because of the Metis, but me may be one continent away. </div> </div> </div>This is probably at least true on the slur side of things. A lot of my Canadian RPG friends were really turned off by it. The disability as divine punishment angle is something I've seen negative reactions to on a much more geographically diverse level.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> By the way, Onyx Path offered us /the writers a tool to change the Metis, namely Shattered Dreams. </div> </div> </div>Which WW said isn't canon, and it seems doubtful that anything in it will be incorporated into W5.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illithid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1310698#post1310698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But then you are punishing the mother for the sexual act, there will be an issue with that if it's the direction they take too.</div> </div> </div> </div>So do what happens to the Kitsune where both parents feel the pain of breaking the taboo. The point remains that there's no necessity to the specific execution of the Metis as they currently stand.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Deformities, There has been a bit of a movement to stop tying monstrousness with real-life disabilities. More so in D&amp;D and similar fantasy, but it could be an issue. I've not actually talked to anyone affected personally. Can this be resolved by only having supernatural and not-disability-representing options for the Metis? </div> </div> </div>I don't think so. People with disabilities aren't going to be mollified if you just make the disabilities all fluffed super magical. Demonizing disabilities is a problem. Demonizing fantastical disabilities doesn't really address the issue.<br /> <br /> The general advice is &quot;don't punch down.&quot; If all you're doing is making up fictional things to punch down on... you're still punching down. No matter how fantasy you make the deformity, as long as deformity comes from sin, you're saying disabled people deserve it because their parents are bad people. The problem isn't that deformities exist; or even that they closely resemble real world disabilities. It's why they happen the way they happen that needs to be addressed.<br /> <br /> Two subtle things about my initial suggestion along these lines:<br /> <br /> 1) It postulates that the natural state is that Garou can love and mate with other Garou, and their children would be normal (for born werewolves). Those instincts were never lost, even as the Garou cursed themselves to curb Metis births. Your parents didn't sin, the violated a bad taboo that happens to have supernatural backing behind it.<br /> <br /> 2) If the Garou caused it... the Garou can undo it. <br /> <br /> The current state of the Metis locks things in a status quo of punching down. The Metis are divinely ordained to be the way they are, so the Garou (and thus the players) feel justified in treating them that way. There isn't a set hook for fighting this successfully even if most Garou raised during recorded history would never be progressive enough to try (enter the PCs).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What if the spirits punish the parents of a Metis with marks showing they broke the litany instead of the Metis itself? </div> </div> </div>It's probably a good idea either way; or at least some variant on it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> *However, W5 will likely be created with Video games and LARP compatibility in mind (Considering Paradox Interactive) so it may be influenced by BNS Larp versions of what's going on with Metis and the spiritually unawakened werewolves... </div> </div> </div>BNS WtA didn't really change much with the Metis. The Bitten are a new thing, that muddy the conceptual waters of the Metis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-08T19:09:35-07:00","id":1310874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1310702#post1310702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So do what happens to the Kitsune where both parents feel the pain of breaking the taboo. The point remains that there's no necessity to the specific execution of the Metis as they currently stand.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a big difference between punishing just the mother or both parents; I'm all for punishing both, but punishing just the mother would be ... problematic<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1310702#post1310702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think so. People with disabilities aren't going to be mollified if you just make the disabilities all fluffed super magical. Demonizing disabilities is a problem. Demonizing fantastical disabilities doesn't really address the issue.<br /> <br /> The general advice is &quot;don't punch down.&quot; If all you're doing is making up fictional things to punch down on... you're still punching down. No matter how fantasy you make the deformity, as long as deformity comes from sin, you're saying disabled people deserve it because their parents are bad people. The problem isn't that deformities exist; or even that they closely resemble real world disabilities. It's why they happen the way they happen that needs to be addressed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I Agree, Punching up is Satire, Punching down is bullying.<br /> My perspective on disabilities in Fantasy roleplaying is mostly from articles I read, and the take away (From that author) was that people had issue with real disabilities being used to describe &quot;monstrous&quot; races (D&amp;D) and that it was ok to use different things that are real-world disabilities.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1310702#post1310702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The current state of the Metis locks things in a status quo of punching down. The Metis are divinely ordained to be the way they are, so the Garou (and thus the players) feel justified in treating them that way. There isn't a set hook for fighting this successfully even if most Garou raised during recorded history would never be progressive enough to try (enter the PCs).</div> </div> </div> </div>There's still things like the social penalties for Bone Gnawers due to their &quot;Homeless&quot; stereotype, which is punching down. There's quite a bit of it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","name":"Illithid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16927_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-08T19:15:01-07:00","id":1310876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illithid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1310874#post1310874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a big difference between punishing just the mother or both parents; I'm all for punishing both, but punishing just the mother would be ... problematic</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, the problem is that other Garou don't inherently know who the father is. This is kind of a thing through history and literature. It wouldn't be unusual for the mother's punishment to depend on whether or not she's willing to name the father.<br /> <br /> I mean we're not going to suggest that Hawthorn was SUPPORTING Hester's treatment, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 05-08-2019, 10:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-08T19:24:43-07:00","id":1310882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1310876#post1310876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right, the problem is that other Garou don't inherently know who the father is. This is kind of a thing through history and literature. It wouldn't be unusual for the mother's punishment to depend on whether or not she's willing to name the father.</div> </div> </div> </div>Socially, absolutely. If we're looking at a Spirit backed issue, then that doesn't matter, the spirits can track it down","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","name":"Illithid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16927_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-08T20:15:14-07:00","id":1310898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illithid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1310874#post1310874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a big difference between punishing just the mother or both parents; I'm all for punishing both, but punishing just the mother would be ... problematic<br /> ...<br /> There's still things like the social penalties for Bone Gnawers due to their &quot;Homeless&quot; stereotype, which is punching down. There's quite a bit of it</div> </div> </div> </div>OK... what's up with this?<br /> <br /> Is there a reason you're doing the whole, &quot;But what about problem X? Huh?&quot; shtick? There is no moral, ethical, or game design reason why we have to address every problematic thing in the game at the same time. We can talk about the problems with the Metis as they are currently written without constantly pointing out to the other shit the game does poorly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-08T20:36:41-07:00","id":1310904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1310898#post1310898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;But what about problem X? Huh?&quot; shtick? There is no moral, ethical, or game design reason why we have to address every problematic thing in the game at the same time. We can talk about the problems with the Metis as they are currently written without constantly pointing out to the other shit the game does poorly.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not a schtick, just the conversational impulse that came to mind that if the main aspect of Metis is worrying about &quot;Punching down&quot; then that should be addressed across the board (Not looking at ALL issues with the game)<br /> But, you're right, focusing on Metis doesn't require a look on other aspects at this time. Thank you for bringing me up on it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","name":"Illithid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16927_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-08T21:46:15-07:00","id":1310920,"title":"","content":"I remember something from 1st or 2nd edition saying more then a few fathers don't want to acknowledge a Metis<br /> <br /> <br /> others Give out (Often times false) Confessions of rape, hoping to shield her.<br /> <br /> in either case...<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-09T05:46:48-07:00","id":1310961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1310702#post1310702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Metis are unique because they only exist because Gaia either lets them exist, or actively caused them to exist.<br /> Metis is a sin that's really the Garou's fault instead of Gaia's fault.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's we don't know. And that's a part what you/we ignore. A Metis is born deformed. That's for sure. But we don't realy know why. The Garou-society thinks that this is a punishent, but it can be becouse of some supernatural-mundane cases on which they (I mean Gartou) attached legends and taboos.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1310702#post1310702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> But one that the spirits actively support. There's no spiritual repercussions for being a dick to a Metis like there would be for mistreating other Garou. The Garou might not have to do it, but unless they're serving a small few very specific Totems, there's nothing stopping them from doing it; even as there are mechanisms to punish them for all sorts of other shitty behavior.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nay, or at least depends on the ST. I personaly punish those, who actively messes with Metis, but yes, their other deeds can cover those penalties. Just some exmaples, from the &quot;official&quot; charts:<br /> <br /> Participating in an unjust challenge: Challenge a Metis to shame him in combat.<br /> Falsely accusing a Garou of being &quot;of the Wyrm: No explanation needed.<br /> Being disrespectful during a rite (depends on the severity): Giggling during \u201ePurple Worm\u201d\u2019s Rite of Passage.<br /> Using a fetish for selfish reasons only: Using it to punish a Metis unnecessary.<br /> Failing to perform regular duties and chores for the sept (subtracted at monthly Moot rite): Don\u2019t give them the Metis the same access to the researches (teaching; weapon; bunk; food; etc.) as others.<br /> Breaking the Litany:<br /> - Accept an Honorable Surrender: Kicking the crying metis pup in the gut to show superiority.<br /> - Submission to Those of Higher Station: Not showing respect to a Metis Elder, because of you are a Pure Breed Silver Fang pup with lineage back to Ivan Tzarevits.<br /> - Respect Those of Lower Station, for all are of Gaia.: Nuff have to be said.<br /> <br /> It says nowhere (as far as I remember) that those rules doesn't apply with Metis.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1310702#post1310702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does that really matter to the point of punishing the parent who sinned instead of the child that did nothing wrong?</div> </div> </div> </div>They *think* it's a punisment. It could be a much fruitable RPG opportunity to CHANGE, during play or during the metaplot the predisposition against the metis then censure it. That's my *oppinion*.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1310702#post1310702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The chance would probably be better without the spirits enforcing this whole Metis thing...</div> </div> </div> </div>I never found any reference that the spirits does this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1310702#post1310702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...how poorly the Garou were created to maximize that chance instead of minimizing it.</div> </div> </div> </div>There were multiple references that the Garou were infected with the power of the Wyrm which drive them towards d*ckheadness.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1310702#post1310702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you're making perfect the enemy of good here. First, fictional worlds are generally more resilient than you're giving credit, and second retcons are something you can use a new edition to execute to be as minimally disruptive as possible. In the 15+ of metaplot that's going to have happened before the end of WtA Rev. and the start of W5, it's extremely easy to finesse in some retcons along the lines I was mentioning earlier.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hating retcons is just my insignificant judgement. Maybe it can be done well.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1310702#post1310702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So do what happens to the Kitsune where both parents feel the pain of breaking the taboo.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is no such a taboo there.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1310702#post1310702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The general advice is &quot;don't punch down.&quot; If all you're doing is making up fictional things to punch down on... you're still punching down.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wolves punches down, people punches down, life punches down.I don't like it, I trie to change it, and be a good dog, but unfortunately, that's a fact. WW started out as a dark, unforgiving, biased, racist, etc. shade of our world. When I start to ST it to new players I always emphatise it it won't be fair, and they will s*ck (I NEVER USE IT TO HURT PLAYERS PERSONALY, just to mention). Some of them leave, much like it. The grimeness make the (tragic) heroes bright lighter. I like WW opressing, some don't.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1310702#post1310702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Metis are divinely ordained to be the way they are, so the Garou (and thus the players) feel justified in treating them that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nay, the legends are not divine law.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1310702#post1310702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There isn't a set hook for fighting this successfully even if most Garou raised during recorded history would never be progressive enough to try (enter the PCs).</div> </div> </div> </div>Children of Gaia and some Totems say otherwise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":562,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/562-lachdanan","user":"Lachdanan","date":". 05-09-2019, 08:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/562-lachdanan","name":"Lachdanan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-09T11:04:29-07:00","id":1311015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lachdanan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1310961#post1310961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's we don't know. And that's a part what you/we ignore.</div> </div> </div> </div>Everything I posted is something we do know. We know that being a shifter doesn't require the answer to &quot;two shifters of the same type bone, what happens,&quot; to be, &quot;a deformed sterile cursed child.&quot; The majority of shifters don't have this happen to them. Whatever spiritual process that created the changing breeds isn't one that either inherently imbues this aspect on them, or if it does, the majority of them were somehow shielded from it.<br /> <br /> We know it must be the case that either the Garou were made this way, or a power with the ability to block it didn't. Even if the books don't say that explicitly, it's the only logical conclusions from the facts as presented.<br /> <br /> Just shouting &quot;We don't know!&quot; doesn't highlight anything important, it makes you look like you're grasping at straws to keep a debate going.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A Metis is born deformed. That's for sure. But we don't realy know why. The Garou-society thinks that this is a punishent, but it can be becouse of some supernatural-mundane cases on which they (I mean Gartou) attached legends and taboos. </div> </div> </div>Maybe don't ignore the paragraph between those two sentences and the specific word choice I used if you want to make a cogent counterpoint.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Nay, or at least depends on the ST. I personaly punish those, who actively messes with Metis, but yes, their other deeds can cover those penalties. </div> </div> </div>Then you're toeing the line of just house ruling the game to be nicer to the Metis than it is.<br /> <br /> A good number of your examples are Renown losses for disrespecting Garou customs and culture to spite a Metis. If an Elder tells you to stop, and you run up and kick a Metis while they're down anyway, getting punished for disobeying an Elder is because you disobeyed an Elder, not because you picked on a Metis.<br /> <br /> The Litany examples are all twisted. Accepting surrender in Garou society frequently comes with a display of dominance; like grabbing the other Garou by the throat. The whole display is, &quot;I could easily kill you, this hurts a bit to show it, but I'm going to accept your surrender instead.&quot; So causing a bit more pain or humiliation isn't a Litany breach as long as the surrender is honored. Submission and respect aren't the same thing. Respect those beneath you is clearly not something the spirits think means, 'treat everyone as equals,' but rather, 'don't treat people worse than you should.' and the books make it pretty clear that bullying Metis isn't disrespecting them because the spirits allow this cultural practice to be part of their 'proper' standing in Garou society so you're not disrespecting them; just like you're not breaking the Litany when you treat Kin like slaves.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They *think* it's a punisment. It could be a much fruitable RPG opportunity to CHANGE, during play or during the metaplot the predisposition against the metis then censure it. </div> </div> </div>The game lacks any hooks for that change in play, and we're talking about changing it in W5, which means changing it with a mix of retcons and metaplot (aka the metaplot revealing the retcons).<br /> <br /> I'd also like to know if you mean censure or censor because my response to that aspect of your comment would change significantly based on that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's my *oppinion*. </div> </div> </div>That's nice. So what?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I never found any reference that the spirits does this. </div> </div> </div>The spirits enforce the Litany, including the first tenant of it. So, yeah, there's plenty of references to this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There were multiple references that the Garou were infected with the power of the Wyrm which drive them towards d*ckheadness. </div> </div> </div>Do we know that actually happened? Care to cite something, or actually go through the steps of why this is necessary from the other facts in evidence? Or just arguing two contrary positions because you seem to care more about trying to poke holes in my posts than coming up with something useful to say?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There is no such a taboo there. </div> </div> </div>Yes, I know. I mentioned that earlier even. Try to not ignore earlier parts of a post when responding to later ones?<br /> <br /> I assumed that after my whole bit about how few of the Fera have Metis, it was safe to save a few words. So to be clear, I felt the following inferences didn't need overt statements, but if you're in nitpick until you can feel like you've done something good mode, here:<br /> <br /> &quot;So do [to the Garou] what happens to the Kitsune where both [Garou] parents [would] feel the pain of breaking the taboo [for them].&quot;<br /> <br /> Do you feel better making me add words that seemed to be clear without that?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Wolves punches down, people punches down, life punches down... </div> </div> </div>You're missing the point. &quot;Punching down&quot; is for authors/creators/us/etc.not the fictional characters. Fictional characters can be as horrible as necessary for the story/setting. The point of punching up, not down, is to make sure that the story that you're telling isn't about reinforcing that stuff instead of fighting against it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (I NEVER USE IT TO HURT PLAYERS PERSONALY, just to mention). </div> </div> </div>You never do so intentionally. If players have walked on you, I assure you have you do it incidentally and the lack of care you seem to have about that is... not endearing to say the least.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The grimeness make the (tragic) heroes bright lighter. </div> </div> </div>And the Metis are one of the areas were the grim aspect of the WoD strays into grim-dark as it offers no light for the characters to achieve.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Nay, the legends are not divine law. </div> </div> </div>Both, actually, read the books maybe?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Children of Gaia and some Totems say otherwise. </div> </div> </div>Some CoG say otherwise and have never shown a single reason to believe they have something beyond stubborn belief in it as the white middle class savior wannabes they are, and no Totems say otherwise; a few just say not to be suck dicks about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-11T14:01:19-07:00","id":1311433,"title":"","content":"Yeah, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> you got me there with the point on no one wanting to actually fix the metis condition.<br /> <br /> That is actually really interesting, as it implies that while a lot of garou accept the breed, they still think they sort of deserve to be like that. I mean, yeah, kinfolk and all that. But it is a good thing that could be more discussed in the setting. Rather than just assumed as a sad truth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-11T21:12:00-07:00","id":1311498,"title":"","content":"It occurs to me that while the majority of Fera have their Litany handed down from Word of God or some equivalent, the Garou do not. The Litany seems more or less in response to the things they did intially.(The Hakken even going so far as to apparently ignore it having broken away long ago)<br /> <br /> I think this adds a certain credence to the idea that Metis deformity is caused by something Garou did. The Apis did seem to have options that would let them mitigate much of the issue.. so what if the break was the death of the apis? It would explain why some other breeds are at least partially effected by the issue...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-12T15:36:27-07:00","id":1311621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1311498#post1311498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It occurs to me that while the majority of Fera have their Litany handed down from Word of God or some equivalent, the Garou do not. The Litany seems more or less in response to the things they did intially.(The Hakken even going so far as to apparently ignore it having broken away long ago)<br /> <br /> I think this adds a certain credence to the idea that Metis deformity is caused by something Garou did. The Apis did seem to have options that would let them mitigate much of the issue.. so what if the break was the death of the apis? It would explain why some other breeds are at least partially effected by the issue...</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically, if the Apis were still around guiding them on breeding, it wouldn't be an issue either way... <br /> For games that delve in to the history, or fixing the Metis, maybe those with issues with Metis could have been cursed by the Apis as a death cry; or the Wyrm could have got it's tentacles in them at the point they destroyed the last Apis? Each of the Fera cursed in respect of their involvement for the genocide.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","name":"Illithid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16927_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-12T16:34:57-07:00","id":1311632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition#post1310339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So let us say that you get to decide some aspect of the (to be) 5th edition, mainly the breeds. You still want homid and lupus to be there, but what about metis?<br /> <br /> Here I move to the meat of this thread. If WtA faces the kind of heavy restructuring that Vampire went under, should the metis breed still remain in the game?<br /> <br /> For one, what message does it send to the players that the garouxgarou child is a deformed and infertile creature, named rather poorly as metis? This isn't 90s anymore, we are more aware of players who are disabled. Or what about the actual Canadian metis people?<br /> <br /> Then there is the fact that metis have zero actual werewolf myth role. They are very much a combination of <a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/TheGrotesque\" target=\"_blank\">The Grotesque</a> and <a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/MadwomanInTheAttic\" target=\"_blank\">Madwoman in the Attic </a>tropes. Not as much on anything werewolf myths have.<br /> <br /> Then again, metis serve as a good example of garou pride and arrogance, not to mention moral blindness. They are very much the example how dark garou society can be at times.<br /> <br /> What do you guys think?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I never liked the idea that Werewolves were forbidden to mate with each other in the first place. I get the idea behind trying to portray it as some form of incest, but that concept was hilariously idiotic from the get-go.<br /> <br /> If I could rewrite the Metis, I'd just make them a breed that are naturally born in their warform, but I would omit all the inbred mutations. I think walking around in a form that is specifically designed to kill everything within arm's reach is already enough of a massive handicap, that you don't need to add physical deformities and mental impairment on top of it. The fact that they leave behind a gigantic red flag that could shatter the masquerade (or whatever the Werewolf equivalent is) when they die should provide all the incentive for the Garou to avoid trying to mate with each other.<br /> <br /> Although, if W5 is taking place during the Apocalypse, just as V5 is taking place during Gehenna, I could see a scenario involving the Metis becoming more numerous in recent years, as the Garou become increasingly more desperate to increase their numbers in the fight against the Wyrm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 05-12-2019, 07:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-12T16:53:20-07:00","id":1311637,"title":"","content":"The problem is that making Metis to increase their numbers never made sense when you can breed wolves. The risk of &quot;taming&quot; wolf kin by putting them in breeding programs is significantly low when you consider their gestation time, litter size, rate of development, and not having the complications of Metis pregnancies, birth, or deformities...it's by far the fastest way to get as many Garou as possible.<br /> <br /> A high PB wolf, and a high PB Garou, can pop out 0-2 high PB Garou and 3-7 high PB wolf kin. Every year. For probably around 6 fertile years. Wolves reach physical maturity (And thus tend to First Change) within two years.<br /> <br /> With Metis taking longer to reach First Change age than Lupus... there's no reason to try to shore up numbers ASAP with Metis when Homid and Lupus Garou can both reproduce with wolves.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-12T17:10:21-07:00","id":1311642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1311637#post1311637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem is that making Metis to increase their numbers never made sense when you can breed wolves. The risk of &quot;taming&quot; wolf kin by putting them in breeding programs is significantly low when you consider their gestation time, litter size, rate of development, and not having the complications of Metis pregnancies, birth, or deformities...it's by far the fastest way to get as many Garou as possible.<br /> <br /> A high PB wolf, and a high PB Garou, can pop out 0-2 high PB Garou and 3-7 high PB wolf kin. Every year. For probably around 6 fertile years. Wolves reach physical maturity (And thus tend to First Change) within two years.<br /> <br /> With Metis taking longer to reach First Change age than Lupus... there's no reason to try to shore up numbers ASAP with Metis when Homid and Lupus Garou can both reproduce with wolves.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> A valid point. But you're forgetting that Metis are naturally born in hybrid form. Which means that they don't need to undergo the First Change, before they're ready to take up arms against the Wyrm. They're ready to kill from the moment they can crawl.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-12T17:46:55-07:00","id":1311656,"title":"","content":"They have claws and fangs from the moment they're born. They're not fully developed (aka having the high stats we associate with adults in Crinos), and have no combat training. It takes time for a Metis to mature enough to even consider sending into a fight even if you do it before they fully change the first time. And wolves have the same basic advantage. Wolves need to hunt to kill and eat. By two years old, a Lupus Garou is probably a more experienced killer than a Metis cub is at five.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-12T17:54:43-07:00","id":1311660,"title":"","content":"That does depend on how many female wolf kin you think exist of high PB... and a couple of tribes don't have that option at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-12T19:09:31-07:00","id":1311679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1311642#post1311642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A valid point. But you're forgetting that Metis are naturally born in hybrid form. Which means that they don't need to undergo the First Change, before they're ready to take up arms against the Wyrm. They're ready to kill from the moment they can crawl.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're still a child mentally, at 8 years old they have the First change, signifying adolescence. Now, you could send them in to combat earlier, but we're looking at issues of morality similar to Child-soldiers","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","name":"Illithid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16927_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-12T21:06:17-07:00","id":1311700,"title":"","content":"Plus let us remember that metis deformities are random, you literally cannot predict if the kid gets horns or brittle bones. Or that a metis pregnancy is full 9 months to wolves' 2, the mother might not survive or becomes infertile. Also, metis at MOST come in twins, lupus produce more pups per litter.<br /> <br /> The mass-production of metis is slow and you are likely to lose 1 garou per pup. The wait time for that pup to grow enough to be useful is also wayyyyy longer than with lupus pups.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-12T21:19:19-07:00","id":1311703,"title":"","content":"Would like to say Im autistic, and Have MS And I think that Metis are an important part of the Werewolf experience.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-12T21:32:23-07:00","id":1311706,"title":"","content":"For me, there's one thing that stops breeding out Lupis compared to breeding out Metis for repopulating...<br /> <br /> Maybe my mindset would change as Garou, but as a Homid, I don't like the idea of having sex with a wolf, or mongrel wolf-dog since i'd realistically be Glasswalker or Bone Gnawer.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","name":"Illithid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16927_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-12T22:03:13-07:00","id":1311709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illithid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1311706#post1311706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For me, there's one thing that stops breeding out Lupis compared to breeding out Metis for repopulating...<br /> <br /> Maybe my mindset would change as Garou, but as a Homid, I don't like the idea of having sex with a wolf, or mongrel wolf-dog since i'd realistically be Glasswalker or Bone Gnawer.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Canonically, homids breeding with wolf-kin is a thing. But honestly, there are lupus garou as well. But yeah, despite what I've seen over the years, generally garou do not see regular wolves as just animal, as they ARE part wolf as well as human. Like lupus garou can see homid kin as potential mates.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-13T00:25:25-07:00","id":1311721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1311015#post1311015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Just shouting &quot;We don't know!&quot; doesn't highlight anything important, it makes you look like you're grasping at straws to keep a debate going.</div> </div> </div> </div>No one shouts. I'd just like to emphasize that the Metis-problem can be divinely-ordered, but there are not proofs. You strongly advocates on this, but you can give as as much proof about it than me saying it's not.<br /> By the way we know that Gaia is not all powerful, so she could make her creation with involuntary flaws. Metis condition could be such thing. During a metaplot line (such one seen in Oprheus) that condition could be alleviated with heroic deeds of PC and that would be more meaningful than a retcon.<br /> <br /> Some game lines already started small living campaigns where the gamer\u2019s feedback affect the next products. Alleviating the Metis-condition could be done during such a process and with it the WW could be sure to incorporate the Players expectations.<br /> <br /> But to start such an endeavor they should clarify the cause of Metis condition. If it\u2019s Gaia\u2019s will, how make her change it? Is it a genetic quirk? How to treat it? If both, because Garou coexist in a material-spiritual world, how to address them together?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1311015#post1311015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Maybe don't ignore the paragraph between those two sentences and the specific word choice I used if you want to make a cogent counterpoint.</div> </div> </div> </div>English is just my second language. Sometimes I miss parts/nuances or misinterpret. Here I refered to their existences as divine ordination.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1311015#post1311015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The Litany examples are all twisted.</div> </div> </div> </div> Maybe yes. The Renown losses were always a subjective matter.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1311015#post1311015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The game lacks any hooks for that change in play, and we're talking about changing it in W5, which means changing it with a mix of retcons and metaplot (aka the metaplot revealing the retcons).<br /> <br /> I'd also like to know if you mean censure or censor because my response to that aspect of your comment would change significantly based on that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, back to my language problem: Censure.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1311015#post1311015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The spirits enforce the Litany, including the first tenant of it. So, yeah, there's plenty of references to this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Spirits does lot of things, Renown losses, loosing Rank, tieing your solaces together, but there is no reference anywhere that the Metis condition, and I mean the disfigurements here are made by the spirits.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1311015#post1311015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do we know that actually happened? Care to cite something, or actually go through the steps of why this is necessary from the other facts in evidence?</div> </div> </div> </div>It depends if you/we accept the novels as official source. If yes the \u201eHearthsplinter\u201d Talon is a good start.<br /> If not, the Rage section, and the \u201eThrall of the Wyrm\u201d is also strongly suggest the Wyrm-touch.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1311015#post1311015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or just arguing two contrary positions because you seem to care more about trying to poke holes in my posts than coming up with something useful to say?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sorry, argument is a personal flaw of mine.<br /> You have a strong standpoint about the reasons of this matter. That\u2019s what I wanted to dispute. It\u2019s nothing personal and if I upset or angered you, I\u2019m sorry. It wasn\u2019t my intention.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1311015#post1311015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you feel better making me add words that seemed to be clear without that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Longer: It wasn\u2019t clear for me, as I said I\u2019m a non-native English speaker.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1311015#post1311015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2026make sure that the story that you're telling isn't about reinforcing that stuff instead of fighting against it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I totally agree.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1311015#post1311015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You never do so intentionally. If players have walked on you, I assure you have you do it incidentally and the lack of care you seem to have about that is... not endearing to say the least. ?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You don\u2019t know me, don\u2019t go into personal.<br /> <br /> Longer: Many players come from different game-lines. Lot\u2019s of them come from high-fantasy games and don\u2019t like struggling or even minor setbacks. They want to shine in armors, waving flaming swords and kill dragons. For them the games (and I thing WoD) I tell doesn\u2019t fit, so they move. There are other cases, but I think every ST lost some of the would be gamers because of some reasons. If you haven\u2019t I envy you.<br /> <br /> What I can say don\u2019t force obnoxious topics to make my players feel bad or uncomfortable.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1311015#post1311015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the Metis are one of the areas were the grim aspect of the WoD strays into grim-dark as it offers no light for the characters to achieve.</div> </div> </div> </div>It depends on the ST and players. Maybe the players won\u2019t change the whole society, they won\u2019t abolish the deformities, but I saw players who, against all odds:<br /> - Found humanity in himself and adopted two Metis children to have a dysfunctional but loving family.<br /> - Sacrificed herself to save her pack and Caern and become a minor legend, causing the septmates to treat other Metis a little better.<br /> - Lived up to every standard, accepted every hardship to cause his father (who abandoned her mother and him) to accept him as his child and suffer punishment for breaking the Litany.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1311015#post1311015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Both, actually, read the books maybe?</div> </div> </div> </div> Again, don\u2019t be personal. We have different viewpoints, but don\u2019t try to shame me. I\u2019ve read them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1311656#post1311656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They have claws and fangs from the moment they're born. They're not fully developed (aka having the high stats we associate with adults in Crinos), and have no combat training. It takes time for a Metis to mature enough to even consider sending into a fight even if you do it before they fully change the first time. And wolves have the same basic advantage. Wolves need to hunt to kill and eat. By two years old, a Lupus Garou is probably a more experienced killer than a Metis cub is at five.</div> </div> </div> </div>Arms are right. Add the problem of inherent Rage and poor impulse control.<br /> It\u2019s clear that more potential lies in lupus-breeding (and it doesn\u2019t have to domestication program) programs than in breeding Metis.<br /> The only problem is the wolves are more vulnerable to predation of the Garous\u2019 foes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illithid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1311706#post1311706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For me, there's one thing that stops breeding out Lupis compared to breeding out Metis for repopulating...<br /> <br /> Maybe my mindset would change as Garou, but as a Homid, I don't like the idea of having sex with a wolf, or mongrel wolf-dog since i'd realistically be Glasswalker or Bone Gnawer.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The \u201ebestiality\u201d problem came up more than once on these forums. Some of my players abhored the idea, some of them didn\u2019t show any revulsion.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/562-lachdanan","name":"Lachdanan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-13T02:18:47-07:00","id":1311733,"title":"","content":"Bleh, lost a big post. Anyway... probably not worth it:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar16927_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"16927\" data-vbnamecard=\"16927\">Illithid</a> <br /> <br /> OK, you're thinking as a human and breeding with a non-human. Spend some time thinking as a person with a uterus being asked (or worse) to go through a Metis pregnancy because people with penises don't want their forced breeding program to make them feel icky when they have sex with a wolf.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/562-lachdanan\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar562_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"562\" data-vbnamecard=\"562\">Lachdanan</a> <br /> <br /> I find your protestations of English not being a native language spurious at best. It seems to be a regular pattern in this debate of your using whatever excuses you can to end a line of discussion when it seems to be not going in a way you like.<br /> <br /> Despite severely misquoting me - including cutting out a huge amount of a passage and altering the last sentence in a fashion that radically changes the meaning by cutting out just the right words - in a fashion that happens to let you argue what you want to argue against, instead of what I actually said, you want me to believe it's just a language barrier. You say you are conscious of miscommunications but have made multiple assertions based on interpretations that suit you rather than asking for clarifications. You want to use yourself as an example, but you call foul about me going personal when I comment on what you bring up about yourself.<br /> <br /> Nope. Not buying it. At all. Peddle your self-serving lapses in English to someone else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-13T02:36:01-07:00","id":1311736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1311700#post1311700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plus let us remember that metis deformities are random, you literally cannot predict if the kid gets horns or brittle bones. Or that a metis pregnancy is full 9 months to wolves' 2, the mother might not survive or becomes infertile. Also, metis at MOST come in twins, lupus produce more pups per litter.<br /> <br /> The mass-production of metis is slow and you are likely to lose 1 garou per pup. The wait time for that pup to grow enough to be useful is also wayyyyy longer than with lupus pups.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hence why I would toss out the idea of them having deformities in the first place. Simply by virtue of being in Crinos form by default, they already have enough problems to deal with.<br /> <br /> But I suppose the wolf born would also satisfy the criteria of being natural born killers. They are carnivorous animals, after all.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit:</b> The reason why I don't agree with the whole &quot;inbred mutation&quot; angle with Metis is because there is absolutely no rational ground for why it should exist. First of all, Werewolves are divided up into many different tribes, who have their own cultural views about things. Even if I was generous and said that Metis deformities happen when two members of the same tribe breed together, this could easily be fixed by having the Garou breed across different tribes. This would also help to promote good relationships between the tribes, so that they can focus on their primary mission.<br /> <br /> Second of all, science tells us that every human on the planet is distantly related to each other in some fashion or another. Going by Werewolf logic, humans shouldn't be allowed to mate with other humans, because that's incest!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 05-13-2019, 05:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-13T04:55:56-07:00","id":1311754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1311736#post1311736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The reason why I don't agree with the whole &quot;inbred mutation&quot; angle with Metis is because there is absolutely no rational ground for why it should exist. First of all, Werewolves are divided up into many different tribes, who have their own cultural views about things. Even if I was generous and said that Metis deformities happen when two members of the same tribe breed together, this could easily be fixed by having the Garou breed across different tribes. This would also help to promote good relationships between the tribes, so that they can focus on their primary mission.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is why I made this thread, because the sole reason Metis are deformed and sterile by setting themes, is due to them being children of incest and to avoid garou breeding with one another. Everything in their design says 'inbred freak child hidden in the Caern from people.' There is no werewolf myth themed reason to fall back on, and that is important when it comes to reconstructuring the setting.<br /> <br /> Forsaken dropped the unihar, because werewolves not breeding with one another due to a disabled child wasn't as impactful as in WtA. Not to mention, it also created a very kinfolk-like situation for the Wolf-Blooded that possibly was not intended.<br /> <br /> With future WtA, the writers have to look at the setting and really think on what themes can stay. The existence of metis might go, due to the very unfortunate implications the breed was build upon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-13T08:55:27-07:00","id":1311792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1310572#post1310572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) It doesn't make sense for the Metis to even be possible. If Gaia truly wants there to be no Garou-Garou mating... why not make it impossible for that to happen?</div> </div> </div> </div>And if she didn't want to die, why doens't she just cure the wyrm?<br /> <br /> If one assumes the Conservation of Energy law applies to magic and well a god creation Creation, then it seems a rule forbidding the mating is more cost efficient than an exception to the rules of procreation of gender based species...<br /> <br /> In any case a law and free will make for better stories. <br /> <br /> Personally I found lupus breed not that helpful to play, for arguments about how a lupus should react or shouldn't when, really, nobody has any experience with the matter. But, if one would remove lupus, metis could be gone too. Much like forsaken. In our LARP game we simply disallowed lupus PCs and rarely a player wants to play a metis.<br /> <br /> And while I think it can be interesting, challanging and rewarding in some ways to play a metis an deal with the additional hardships that come with that, I also feel that neither the other players nor I with my NPCs want to be douchy to a metis all the time. It is exhausting. But if one doesn't live up to the social parts of the metis role it is just a character with a few alternate rules in regards to healing and gift availability. That isn't cool either.<br /> <br /> So, if Stargazers can be removed and put into a supplement book, why can't lupus and metis?<br /> They are still there, but kind of like an advanced theme that one only adds into a chronicle if the players and ST want to deal with that theme.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-13T10:05:38-07:00","id":1311807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1311792#post1311792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Personally I found lupus breed not that helpful to play, for arguments about how a lupus should react or shouldn't when, really, nobody has any experience with the matter. But, if one would remove lupus, metis could be gone too. Much like forsaken. In our LARP game we simply disallowed lupus PCs and rarely a player wants to play a metis.<br /> <br /> And while I think it can be interesting, challanging and rewarding in some ways to play a metis an deal with the additional hardships that come with that, I also feel that neither the other players nor I with my NPCs want to be douchy to a metis all the time. It is exhausting. But if one doesn't live up to the social parts of the metis role it is just a character with a few alternate rules in regards to healing and gift availability. That isn't cool either.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I've always felt people make playing lupus into a much MUCH harder thing than it actually is. Everyone is talking about realism, when basically all you need is to think the lupus as shapeshifting smart wolves. Aside from the shapeshifting part, I have seen people roleplay plain intelligent wolves just fine over the years.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/domain-of-the-wolf/gallery/55911041/Vektren-Pack-Art-and-Literature\" target=\"_blank\">Domain</a><a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/domain-of-the-wolf/gallery/55911041/Vektren-Pack-Art-and-Literature\" target=\"_blank\"> of the Wolf </a>is an art roleplaying game where you play as a wolf trying to live among packs of humanized wolves. While it looks cartoony, it can often get REAL dark with its content, to WoD levels. If these adult people can play mere wolves just fine, what is stopping us from playing lupus who actually ARE half-human? Certainly not more realism, as we are still playing magical werewolves fighting for Earth mother.<br /> <br /> As for metis, I think they serve as an important function in the game. Metis PCs are a very raw reminder that for all the good the Nation does, they still do a lot of systematic wrong. I've found playing metis can be fun to explore these themes, without having other players be bastards to the metis character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-13T11:56:08-07:00","id":1311828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1311792#post1311792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And if she didn't want to die, why doens't she just cure the wyrm?</div> </div> </div> </div>Asked and answered.<br /> <br /> Fera can be made without the ability to make Metis at all, or to make Metis that have no issues with infertility and/or deformities. It's clearly within Gaia's power to see this happen, with no clear logic on which shifters are and aren't stuck with it.<br /> <br /> Personally healing the Triat is something she's never shown to be capable of doing. Making shifters that don't have Metis Breeds is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If one assumes the Conservation of Energy law applies to magic and well a god creation Creation, then it seems a rule forbidding the mating is more cost efficient than an exception to the rules of procreation of gender based species... </div> </div> </div>I... really don't understand what this sentence is trying to say. What are the cost efficiencies involved? What are the &quot;rules of procreation of <u>gender</u> based species to have exceptions too?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In any case a law and free will make for better stories. </div> </div> </div>And execution matters to making better stories. Getting away from the rather obnoxious &quot;deformities are because you exist to shame your sinful parents,&quot; metanarrative makes will make for better stories, and isn't incompatible with &quot;a law and free will.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Personally I found lupus breed not that helpful to play,... </div> </div> </div>Why does that matter here?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, if Stargazers can be removed and put into a supplement book, why can't lupus and metis?<br /> They are still there, but kind of like an advanced theme that one only adds into a chronicle if the players and ST want to deal with that theme. </div> </div> </div>The Stargazers being moved to a supplement is largely regarded as a mistake since it lasted for all of one edition.<br /> <br /> And if you aren't cutting Lupus and Metis from the setting, not putting them in the core book becomes untenable. Forcing people to buy extra books to play 2/3s of the Breeds (even if it's just the ST that's playing them) is not a smart move. And I completely agree with Ana Mizuki on how people vastly over stress playing Lupus. Playing a Lupus is no harder than playing a Homid with decent or high Primal Urge.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1311807#post1311807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for metis, I think they serve as an important function in the game. Metis PCs are a very raw reminder that for all the good the Nation does, they still do a lot of systematic wrong. I've found playing metis can be fun to explore these themes, without having other players be bastards to the metis character.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is the function is redundant. There's lots of options for exploring/keeping focus on the systemic wrongs the Garou Nation does even if you completely cut the Metis. The current state of the Metis is also a good example of how WtA has a tendency to be too heavy handed, then sabotaging it's own themes. By making the hardships of the Metis so extreme, the game ends up giving the anti-Metis bias of the Garou something of a reasonable justification instead of making them look horrible for it. Rather than relying on the weight of cultural inertia and bigotry (which does just fine in perpetuating systemic wrongs), they ended up giving the persecution of Metis reasons that actually require arguing against.<br /> <br /> And as heinrich rightfully points out, playing the NPCs to make the Metis persecution feel real in play can be extremely trying for the ST that has to make it count; esp if the other players aren't going to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-13T15:50:50-07:00","id":1311887,"title":"","content":"The stargazers were never removed from the main book. Revised has them off in theirown little section but they weren't removed from the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-13T19:27:43-07:00","id":1311954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1311733#post1311733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bleh, lost a big post. Anyway... probably not worth it:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar16927_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"16927\" data-vbnamecard=\"16927\">Illithid</a><br /> <br /> OK, you're thinking as a human and breeding with a non-human. Spend some time thinking as a person with a uterus being asked (or worse) to go through a Metis pregnancy because people with penises don't want their forced breeding program to make them feel icky when they have sex with a wolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>Having not been pregnant myself, I wasn't thinking of that aspect, or the birth ... with claws ... <br /> Really it's all a bit off; though - as I did state at the start, maybe being Garou would be different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","name":"Illithid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16927_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-16T05:16:45-07:00","id":1312540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1311828#post1311828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Asked and answered.<br /> <br /> Fera can be made without the ability to make Metis at all, or to make Metis that have no issues with infertility and/or deformities. It's clearly within Gaia's power to see this happen, with no clear logic on which shifters are and aren't stuck with it.<br /> <br /> Personally healing the Triat is something she's never shown to be capable of doing. Making shifters that don't have Metis Breeds is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless the Fera were created by Luna/Helios/Weaver respectively. <br /> Depending on the Order of their Creation, it might have been that some learning involved. Possibly starting with Metis that are deformed, then correcting that, or the other way round.<br /> <br /> Personally I believe that authors of the Fera books just didn't want to deal with Metis and hand-waived the topic or used it to separate their breed from the garou further.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1311828#post1311828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And execution matters to making better stories. Getting away from the rather obnoxious &quot;deformities are because you exist to shame your sinful parents,&quot; metanarrative makes will make for better stories, and isn't incompatible with &quot;a law and free will.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, one could have executed certain matters around the metis theme better. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1311828#post1311828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I completely agree with Ana Mizuki on how people vastly over stress playing Lupus. Playing a Lupus is no harder than playing a Homid with decent or high Primal Urge.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe so. For seasoned characters. But starting characters probably had a year or so since the first change. Meaning for a lupus that they had rational though for about that time. A lot of common knowledge and such is simply unlikely for them to have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-16T06:28:08-07:00","id":1312552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1312540#post1312540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe so. For seasoned characters. But starting characters probably had a year or so since the first change. Meaning for a lupus that they had rational though for about that time. A lot of common knowledge and such is simply unlikely for them to have.</div> </div> </div> </div>And Lupus can't have expended more than a year or so with the tribe learning &quot;a lot of common knowledge&quot; before knowing the pack and <i>actually </i>starting the game?.<br /> <br /> Because in other games the starting character age within the supernatural society isn't that relevant. Neonates can have 20-50 years of being a vampire w/o having different sheets. Experience and capacity aren't a function of age, but of experience. Starting character capacity has to be balanced, all the rest it's just flavor that could justify taking some traits over others, but shouldn't make any character unplayable.<br /> <br /> I think it's far more convinient to say that Lupus had a few years more after the first change in the tribe to adjust and learn stuff (much like young Metis do). The time other Garou races spend after the first change gaining Renown and keeping some ties with human society (like having a job), you expended learning the language and the basics of how to move in society (perhaps even a dot or two in some &quot;modern human&quot; skill you really wanted to learn)...hence you had more than a year after the first change but the same <i>traits and capabilities </i>overal as a starting character...<br /> <br /> Is there some in game reason for why this can't or shouldn't be done?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 05-16-2019, 09:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-16T06:31:36-07:00","id":1312553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1312552#post1312552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a reason Lupus can't have expended time with the tribe learning &quot;a lot of common knowledge&quot; before knowing the pack and starting the game?.</div> </div> </div> </div>They could. But I never read anywhere that they do that (as a general rule). Surely their knowledge restriction wouldn't be that restrictive, if they as a general rule had several years of adjustment and the opportunity to learn between first change and character start.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-16T06:49:11-07:00","id":1312554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1312553#post1312553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They could. But I never read anywhere that they do that (as a general rule). Surely their knowledge restriction wouldn't be that restrictive, if they as a general rule had several years of adjustment and the opportunity to learn between first change and character start.</div> </div> </div> </div>Their knowledge restriction it's quite specific. It involves &quot;modern society&quot; skills that aren't likely to be valued or taught within Garou society. But note that you explicitly CAN expend freebies to learn these skills up to 2 dots in spite of them being utterly alien to wolves (at least in Revised you could, did that change in W20?), and thus a Lupus with Drive would still be a better driver and know more about trafic laws than, say, me (as I don't know anything about that subject). A Lupus with Computer knows more about their PC than the average old person<br /> <br /> More to the point: a Homid character may not have a single dot on those restricted skills either (not rare in certain rural places), so the question would be: Do you feel necessary to make their knowledge more restricted <i>than it already is</i>?. Because if you don't, I don't see how playing them would be worse that playing a Homid w/o the skills in question...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 05-16-2019, 09:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-16T07:02:15-07:00","id":1312559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1312552#post1312552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And Lupus can't have expended more than a year or so with the tribe learning &quot;a lot of common knowledge&quot; before knowing the pack and <i>actually </i>starting the game?.<br /> <br /> Because in other games the starting character age within the supernatural society isn't that relevant. Neonates can have 20-50 years of being a vampire w/o having different sheets. Experience and capacity aren't a function of age, but of experience. Starting character capacity has to be balanced, all the rest it's just flavor that could justify taking some traits over others, but shouldn't make any character unplayable.<br /> <br /> I think it's far more convinient to say that Lupus had a few years more after the first change in the tribe to adjust and learn stuff (much like young Metis do). The time other Garou races spend after the first change gaining Renown and keeping some ties with human society (like having a job), you expended learning the language and the basics of how to move in society (perhaps even a dot or two in some &quot;modern human&quot; skill you really wanted to learn)...hence you had more than a year after the first change but the same <i>traits and capabilities </i>overal as a starting character...<br /> <br /> Is there some in game reason for why this can't or shouldn't be done?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I have always seen cub-hood for lupus as including things like how to NOT break the veil in cities (even the W20 section on Red Talons notes they do this.) The mentality that lupus get rited the -month- they change has always bothered me. Because garou society is far more complex than the wolf one, so how the heck would a lupus even get rited/understand auspice role/tribe, without learning to think more 'human'? Those things aren't instinctual, after all.<br /> <br /> As well as the freebie thing, I've always seen it as the things the lupus learned post-change. They can also have rituals and medicine with their main dots, both which require understanding how to apply their human minds.<br /> <br /> This is basically what I mean by people making playing lupus harder than it should be. They assume lupus don't get ANY training post-change before being rited, so the player must act like they don't get things that a garou would NEED to function as a cliath.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-16T11:07:33-07:00","id":1312603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1312540#post1312540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless the Fera were created by Luna/Helios/Weaver respectively.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh. Not really sure that's a distinction with a difference. Again, when you actually map out where the Fera would fall in this, you don't get a clear picture.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Depending on the Order of their Creation, it might have been that some learning involved. Possibly starting with Metis that are deformed, then correcting that, or the other way round. </div> </div> </div>Well, the &quot;oldest&quot; all seem to be &quot;No Metis.&quot; Though after that it's still a massive jumble. I mean, the explicit youngest (the Kitsune) have Metis, but their Metis are seen as awesome and the only problem is how difficult it is to produce one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Personally I believe that authors of the Fera books just didn't want to deal with Metis and hand-waived the topic or used it to separate their breed from the garou further. </div> </div> </div>Probably? But the even here it's all over the place. And it's not like the order of the Fera getting their books sheds any light on it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1312554#post1312554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But note that you explicitly CAN expend freebies to learn these skills up to 2 dots in spite of them being utterly alien to wolves...</div> </div> </div> </div>In W20 at least, there's no cap on how many freebies you can spend on those. If I want a Lupus PC that starts with Drive 5? It's totally allowable in the rules... it just costs me 10 freebies. Obviously there should be a good ass story behind it too, but nothing stops this.<br /> <br /> Though that's most important for Law and Philodox Lupus because WtA uses Law to cover Garou laws as well as human laws, which means it's the only Auspice that gets hosed by the Lupus restrictions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","user":"Heavy Arms","date":". 05-16-2019, 02:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-15T07:40:21-07:00","id":1402945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1311709#post1311709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Canonically, homids breeding with wolf-kin is a thing. But honestly, there are lupus garou as well. But yeah, despite what I've seen over the years, generally garou do not see regular wolves as just animal, as they ARE part wolf as well as human. Like lupus garou can see homid kin as potential mates.</div> </div> </div> </div> Changing Ways says (on page 90 in the german version) something different. There it is exactly like @<b>Illitith says on post 33. Many Homid Garou begin to think more like humans and less like Garou especially as Glasswalker because for them it would not be natural sex but sex with animals because the wolves only want to breed but the human half want a more emotional connection. There is so the theories that either homids put themselves higher as the wolves because they are with their intelligence better then those mindless wolves or because the garou began to distance themselves from the wolves.<br /> <br /> Though you can put it off as unreliable narrator it is really interesting.<br /> <br /> Anyway about the Metis and the role in the nation I really hope that here in W5 there will be put the modern equality thinking and the first rule of the litany as overhauled because in my group I have three couples and being a romanitc myself I would really look forward if they would write it out.<br /> Mayby with the reason that with how dire the situation is there are not enough wolves anymore to do the ratkin strategy so they breed metis to get guarenteed fighters and/or mayby the come to the enlightment, that resenting Metis and/or their parents cost that them to many of the needed fighters because the metis run over to the wyrm out of resentment and the will to see the world burn because it can not really get worse or to many couples turning ronin because they rather live on their own and taking care of their little family and mayby keeping their district clean but focusing more on having each other safe.<br /> <br /> Really in my round we changed the place to riverdolphin sept in brazil because their they can happily love each other, making reinforcements for the Nation while helping to take care of the Wyrm. The players in my round are argumenting that the litany is totally outdated written like the koran as instructions for complete different time and need to be completely new written and centraly interpretated as an overhaul.</b><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-15T08:32:58-07:00","id":1402952,"title":"","content":"But the first tenet of the Litany isn't overhauled.<br /> <br /> Choosing garou as mates is racist, or speciesist, or what ever - by literally excluding other species.<br /> It has been said by so many garou sages who could see past the Metis deformatiy issue, that this tenet is older than the first metis and that the essence of it is, that the garou must activly pursue human and wolves as partners - besides the Curse making it difficult. For this is tha way the Garou stay in connetction to the world they are to protect.<br /> <br /> I hope, if they make radical changes to the setting, like V5 did, that the will get rid of Metis and lupus period. Forsaken didn't need them and W5 could do without them, too, if there was need for an overhaul. But I hope they won't change anything in the Setting (unless back from W20 to revised), but just mechanics. Figers crossed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-15T08:35:32-07:00","id":1402954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Koronus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1402945#post1402945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Changing Ways says (on page 90 in the german version) something different. There it is exactly like @[B]Illitith says on post 33. Many Homid Garou begin to think more like humans and less like Garou especially as Glasswalker because for them it would not be natural sex but sex with animals because the wolves only want to breed but the human half want a more emotional connection. There is so the theories that either homids put themselves higher as the wolves because they are with their intelligence better then those mindless wolves or because the garou began to distance themselves from the wolves.<br /> <br /> Though you can put it off as unreliable narrator it is really interesting.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I'd take is more seriously, if Changing Ways lupus section (and part of the metis section) didn't clearly try to be shocking. The same page has one of the most bad taste rumours regarding Red Talons and Black Furies. As in, I legit rather not mention it.<br /> <br /> So to me, the 'homids dislike mating with wolf-kin' is trying to imply something most WtA fans have argued against for -years.-","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-15T08:57:28-07:00","id":1402957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1402952#post1402952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the first tenet of the Litany isn't overhauled.<br /> <br /> Choosing garou as mates is racist, or speciesist, or what ever - by literally excluding other species.<br /> It has been said by so many garou sages who could see past the Metis deformatiy issue, that this tenet is older than the first metis and that the essence of it is, that the garou must activly pursue human and wolves as partners - besides the Curse making it difficult. For this is tha way the Garou stay in connetction to the world they are to protect.<br /> <br /> I hope, if they make radical changes to the setting, like V5 did, that the will get rid of Metis and lupus period. Forsaken didn't need them and W5 could do without them, too, if there was need for an overhaul. But I hope they won't change anything in the Setting (unless back from W20 to revised), but just mechanics. Figers crossed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why should be Garou having love with other Garou be racist? It is more the opposite. If your true love happens to be Garou to and your luck and happiness is denied because he whas born as Garou it is racist. You can insert here any other Fera, Vampire or Wraith and it would not change anything on the statement. The problem is, it is only forbidden for heterosexual pairs. Homosexual Garou couples are totally accepted because the Litany do not forbid it and this love happens in nature too. So why is the one love where no children are cumming from good while the love where Metis happens is bad? In some tribes it is even accepted to love other garou in a heterosexual relationship as long there is babymaking so you could for example stick only to oral or analsex and you would be A Okay<br /> This is why the first tennet of the Litany is overhauled. Because it weighs the same thing different.<br /> The litany is really like the first printing of Waboku and Polymerization from Yu-Gi-Oh!. It really needs more explenation to not leave it up for the players/Garou to interpret what it exactly means.<br /> There is even in the Kinfolk A Breed apart another example where the garou came to the conclusion that the litany whas written for a totally different time because the much important homebringing of lost Kinfolk is not part of it because the Litany whas created when the world whas different and so there whas no need for it and would the Litany have come later it would be part of it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-15T09:18:35-07:00","id":1402958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Koronus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1402957#post1402957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why should be Garou having love with other Garou be racist? It is more the opposite. If your true love happens to be Garou to and your luck and happiness is denied because he whas born as Garou it is racist. You can insert here any other Fera, Vampire or Wraith and it would not change anything on the statement. The problem is, it is only forbidden for heterosexual pairs. <b>Homosexual Garou couples are totally accepted </b>because the Litany do not forbid it and this love happens in nature too. So why is the one love where no children are cumming from good while the love where Metis happens is bad? In some tribes it is even accepted to love other garou in a heterosexual relationship as long there is babymaking so you could for example stick only to oral or analsex and you would be A Okay<br /> This is why the first tennet of the Litany is overhauled. Because it weighs the same thing different.<br /> The litany is really like the first printing of Waboku and Polymerization from Yu-Gi-Oh!. It really needs more explenation to not leave it up for the players/Garou to interpret what it exactly means.<br /> There is even in the Kinfolk A Breed apart another example where the garou came to the conclusion that the litany whas written for a totally different time because the much important homebringing of lost Kinfolk is not part of it because the Litany whas created when the world whas different and so there whas no need for it and would the Litany have come later it would be part of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing can stop a philodox from hard -core sept to judge not-acceptable even an homosexual love between garou.<br /> <br /> <br /> Racist and homophobic garou exist as much lgbt and progressive garou exist. Both exist among normal humans, it's logical that they can both exist among a race made for war.<br /> <br /> So, no, it's illogical to say that virtually, ''homosexual garou couples are totally accepted''.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-15T09:48:16-07:00","id":1402961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Helur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1402958#post1402958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nothing can stop a philodox from hard -core sept to judge not-acceptable even an homosexual love between garou.<br /> <br /> <br /> Racist and homophobic garou exist as much lgbt and progressive garou exist. Both exist among normal humans, it's logical that they can both exist among a race made for war.<br /> <br /> So, no, it's illogical to say that virtually, ''homosexual garou couples are totally accepted''.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mayby not totally accepted but the tribes except the Silver Fangs see homosexual releationships between Garou much more positive then heterosexual because &quot;brotherhoodbonding&quot; increases the morale and there is no chance that the litany is violated by sexual intercourse. This is said in Changing Ways on Seite 60 about how the tribes see the Metis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-15T10:00:03-07:00","id":1402963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Koronus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1402961#post1402961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mayby not totally accepted but the tribes except the Silver Fangs see homosexual releationships between Garou much more positive then heterosexual because &quot;brotherhoodbonding&quot; increases the morale and there is no chance that the litany is violated by sexual intercourse. This is said in Changing Ways on Seite 60 about how the tribes see the Metis.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> never said that many septs don't accept them. I just said that as many humans could be racist or homophobic piece of sh*t without even a radical culture, many garou could be as well.<br /> It is also on the storyteller and the players to be ok with the presence of some characters. <br /> Some Fenrir can be really open minded and see in a really positive ways some kind of homosexual camaraderie based on mascluine virtues as much as love between warrior-borthers.<br /> Some other could judge such relationship as a waste of time and force the members of the local tribe to find a kin a mate as much as they can, using homophobia to enforce their duty to breed.<br /> This is just logic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-15T17:18:31-07:00","id":1403014,"title":"","content":"Safespaces as default is a really, really immature way to write a setting. If your players have problems, you can work around them at your table , but making the entire setting for everybody 'safe' on the grounds that someone won't like it? That's the end of art right there. <br /> <br /> Satire is punching up at people who punch down. Satire is about delivering a truth. <br /> <br /> Metis, as they are, belong in the game. Metis, bullied and abused, are important. If we want a mature setting with artistic value, we have to acknowledge the ugly. <br /> <br /> That said, what was done with thinbloods paints an unfortunate picture of what could happen with metis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-15T17:52:56-07:00","id":1403022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1403014#post1403014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Safespaces as default is a really, really immature way to write a setting. If your players have problems, you can work around them at your table , but making the entire setting for everybody 'safe' on the grounds that someone won't like it? That's the end of art right there.<br /> <br /> Satire is punching up at people who punch down. Satire is about delivering a truth.<br /> <br /> Metis, as they are, belong in the game. Metis, bullied and abused, are important. If we want a mature setting with artistic value, we have to acknowledge the ugly.<br /> <br /> That said, what was done with thinbloods paints an unfortunate picture of what could happen with metis.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh we did work with going to one of the two places that in Changing ways whas described for as the opinion of half of the table as &quot;The only sane minds.&quot; but what I ment is, I do not see any In-Logic behind it except showing, that the &quot;good guys&quot; are hypcrit idiots that would turn away good fighters because of something, that whas writen for totally different times.<br /> If you mean this should be critic on how religious fundamentalists hang on the litural meaning of the rule instead of interpret it as for what whas ment for the time, okay point taken.<br /> Though from my Inner World Logic keeping on this rule is totally ignoring the actual state of the world where there are problems without and there are not enough people for everwhere.<br /> Keeping on this Tennent is as effective as putting oneself a silverdagger into the knee and mayby even keep it there.<br /> As I said before with this rule their is legitimate abusing of Garou that mayby are not deformed to badly to fight for the planet. With this tennet you keep Garou from making children and so increasing the ranks of the Garounation because the one they love is sadly another garou which would be illegal. In best case this couple only stops themselves from having children but fight even harder because they have nothing else. In worst case they turn over to the wyrm because the BSD accept it. In the neither totally good nor bad case they run away an get ronins.<br /> Okay you can be like the Silverfangs and saying to breed is the only thing that matters but the rest of the tribes came to the conclusion, that bonding between garou is not a totally bad thing but as long it is homosexuall because then you have not to loose face because of a Metis.<br /> From my point of view there are only two ways out of this madness where you are less punished for having no or non procreation intercourse then where you have one creating a sterile while there are missing fighters on all ends.<br /> First it is the most important duty for every garou to increase so intercourse is only to treat like the Lupis way with fucking for reproduction.<br /> Second the first tennet get disabled because desperate times need desperates measures so if it has to be another Garou to make you do breeding than it have to be.<br /> If you would keep on the first tennet then congratulation, the world ended but at least you punished the rulebreakers.<br /> Hell even if you interpret why this tennet exist, I think you will come to the conclusion, it whas made with the intention, that with Metis being sterile and mayby not so top fighters like other Garou you should breed only with non garou to kill the wyrm while keeping the Garounation alive. Well it whas made while the fight whas not so hopelessly and right if you want to have the nation keep existing you need more Garou. Though while you can do intensive breeding with wolves there are sadly not enough wolves so for all those non wolfbreeders there need to be an alternative and so instead of caring 9 months a human baby that is only with 10% best chance a garou better breed a metis that is 100% garou and hopefully able to fight.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-15T18:13:52-07:00","id":1403025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1403014#post1403014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Safespaces as default is a really, really immature way to write a setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Who is arguing otherwise? The general consensus pre-necro is that the Metis should stay in the game, but need a heavy revision.<br /> <br /> Safe spaces have no part of the issue with using a real world term to describe mixed ancestry people as a term for the cursed children of taboo relations. It has nothing to do with the problem of having the abuse heaped on them be justified by the setting.<br /> <br /> People are free to make whatever art they want. If they make art that pisses people off, well that's their choice to deal with; esp. if they want to profit off of it.<br /> <br /> However much we agree on the value of a certain gaming book, it's art too. By the logic you're putting out, all the criticisms of it are trying to &quot;kill art,&quot; but I doubt you really believe that because you're not really being consistent in your values here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Satire is punching up at people who punch down. Satire is about delivering a truth. </div> </div> </div>You need to make a better case for the Metis as they are then, because as they stands, WtA does not punch up at the people punching down, nor does it deliver an important truth; at least regarding the Metis.<br /> <br /> The abuse of the Metis uses punching down tropes as it is justified by divine curses levied on them for sins of others. It delivers the truth that those born different should be oppressed if religion says so, and that disabilities happen because parents don't follow traditional sexual norms.<br /> <br /> Please show where the games get around to punching up at some point in all this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If we want a mature setting with artistic value, we have to acknowledge the ugly. </div> </div> </div>No, as you note, we need to punch up against the causes of the ugly, not just acknowledge that ugly things exist. We also need to improve the maturity and artistic value of the setting by scrubbing away things that justify and glorify the ideologies that perpetuate that ugly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That said, what was done with thinbloods paints an unfortunate picture of what could happen with metis. </div> </div> </div>I have no love for V5's implementation of thin-bloods, I fail to see what that has to do with how the Metis might be handled. Thin-bloods were vampires with an extra Flaw that V5 tried to turn into a more significant play-style by conflating thin-blood, 14+ Gen, and Caitiff into a new thing. Metis are one of the core splats of WtA.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","user":"Heavy Arms","date":". 07-16-2020, 01:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-16T00:49:56-07:00","id":1403059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1402954#post1402954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So to me, the 'homids dislike mating with wolf-kin' is trying to imply something most WtA fans have argued against for -years.-</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I remember som 20 years ago, when we all were early twenties, a lot of female players in the LARP had their characters have lupus babies between games. Back then the revised rule that cubs always have the mothers breed wasn't enforced in the game and we went with the offspring has the breed of the non-changer parent (which makes more sense in my mind).<br /> <br /> Anyways, as the players grew older, and had real-life babies, this ceased. It wasn't the most rewarding game element anyways.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-16T01:21:11-07:00","id":1403064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Koronus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1402957#post1402957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why should be Garou having love with other Garou be racist?</div> </div> </div> </div>As a general practice, not as a sinvle incident. The garou are forbidden to breed with each other not because of the Metis, although some narrow-minded garou belive that. They are forbidden so the garou wouldn't just hang out amongst themselves.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Koronus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1402957#post1402957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem is, it is only forbidden for heterosexual pairs. Homosexual Garou couples are totally accepted because the Litany do not forbid it and this love happens in nature too.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree. Some newer publications make this point, but there is the whole unreliable narrator thing.<br /> <br /> &quot;When will chieftains realise, that it is about the spritit of a law, and not about its words.&quot; to paraphrase Dschingis Khan.<br /> <br /> When the litany was formed millenia ago, there was not &quot;shall not breed&quot; for English language wasn't even thought of. So don't attribute a meaning to the word, that is narrow, when the tenet was devised to be as broad as possible to bring on board all tribes and breeds, as the legend of the Litany tells us. Also, in German it is called &quot;soll nicht paaren&quot; - as of 2020 the meeting of this has shifted to litterally mean, they should not pair their blutooth devices. Probably a Glass Walker tenet in the Litany against Hackers, you know.<br /> <br /> As far as the Litany description and the legend of its formulation go, there have been and should still be a lot of local stories and legends where garou breeding/loving/pairing has lead to tragedy - even before there was the first Metis. When memeber of all tribes couldn't come up with a code of law to govern them all, the ambacedors traveled to Pangea, where all their tribal characteristics were mystically removed, they managed to distill the Litany tenets we know today (except maybe for the Veil, whoch according to the older Dark Ages book emerged during the Dark Ages).<br /> So, with that in mind, it is fair to assume that all the local septs also have legends about homosexual relationships leading to tragedy, for homosexuallity isn't a new thing.<br /> <br /> So, modern garou may argue about this all the time, but if Philodox and Galliard managed to maintain the old legends that the tenets were derrived from all that millenia ago (or later legends, that also show the validity of the tenets) than the case should be clear - garou/garou pairings are forbidden, period.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Koronus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1402957#post1402957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So why is the one love where no children are cumming from good while the love where Metis happens is bad? In some tribes it is even accepted to love other garou in a heterosexual relationship as long there is babymaking so you could for example stick only to oral or analsex and you would be A Okay</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe, or maybe it is a way to rationalise the breaking of a law - what does that say about honour?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Koronus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1402957#post1402957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is why the first tennet of the Litany is overhauled. Because it weighs the same thing different.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, people interpret it differntly. The wording might not be adequate anymore. The intended meaning, as I layed out, is ageless. You will only apprechiate it in the lupus gnawing language original - or the Klingon version, which conveys the meaning too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Koronus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1402957#post1402957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The litany is really like the first printing of Waboku and Polymerization from Yu-Gi-Oh!. It really needs more explenation to not leave it up for the players/Garou to interpret what it exactly means.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but there is additional information. Besides the in-character definitions in tribe books, there are also out-of-character and in-game (but not in-character) legends in the books. They aren't as prominent as the Litany bits in the TBs, however.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Koronus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1402957#post1402957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is even in the Kinfolk A Breed apart another example where the garou came to the conclusion that the litany whas written for a totally different time because the much important homebringing of lost Kinfolk is not part of it because the Litany whas created when the world whas different and so there whas no need for it and would the Litany have come later it would be part of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe so, BUT there is an important phrase in the revised core, and I think also 2nd, don't know about W20. It states, that there are other local laws and traditions in septs, that have just as high a standing as the Litany. The Litany is just the tenets that some millenia ago the garou could (more or less) agree on as being found in all their local law codexies.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-16T01:23:57-07:00","id":1403065,"title":"","content":"Well, maybe, for W5, all the septs send emmisaries to Pangea again, and come up with newer tenets for the modern world. I wouldn't like that, but seeing how V5 changed it is possible...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-16T02:28:17-07:00","id":1403074,"title":"","content":"I think one of the main challenge playing a metis is exactly to Play an uncomfortable character for the most. I think they should stay ad they are , with some tribes regarding then finally better and some others even worst but I would say that It should specify that the way a metis is treated is also up to the local sept/pack/geographical /cultural situation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-16T03:08:33-07:00","id":1403076,"title":"","content":"What needs to be fixed isn't the &quot;now&quot; Metis (besides addressing the name in some fashion). What needs to be addressed are the past and future of the Metis.<br /> <br /> They need a better in-universe reason for existing from the past to drive a stronger narrative. &quot;We were created with the ability to mate with ourselves, but the same powers-that-be that made us that way curse us and visit suffering on the children if we do,&quot; weakens the game.<br /> <br /> They need a better possible future to fight for to expand what the game can successfully explore. Trying to &quot;heal&quot; the Metis would create the Perfect Metis and bring about the apocalypse. Hard to tell a story about fighting institutionalized discrimination when discrimination is saving the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-16T04:04:27-07:00","id":1403080,"title":"","content":"I think the problem in the game is for one part, that the deities (Gaia, Luna) don't force the garou to treat Metis badly. It is the garou's culture that developed that way...<br /> <br /> Within the game, as a LARPer, I always found that players aren't assholes for the most part and simply don't treat Metis (or Bone Gnawers) as badly as the Setting would dictate. In our game we got rid of all Merits and Flaws that a player doesn't have to protray themselves but that require others to change their portrayal of their character to fit the Merit/Flaw (like Animal Magnetism). On this premise we kind of discurage Metis portrayal, since it brings other players into a conflict between adherence to the Setting and the themes and behaviour they want their character to have/experience.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-16T04:44:16-07:00","id":1403083,"title":"","content":"I think it is a mixture from Garou choosing themselves to treat Metis badly, tribechieftains only trying to listen to exact words and not the spirit like Dschingis Khan is saying, that the apocalypse seems to be 5 before twelve and that so many homids comming from a times where equality and romantic is treated with high value.<br /> <br /> As his Shadowlords character one of my players argued, that the first tennet exist only so that garou do not breed with each other but with the intention, that the world whas in balance so that every Metis would be more a waste because with it being Steril and mayby even to deformed to fight you lost a chance for healthy human or wolf kinfolk that can reproduce and mayby even be another garou. He then followed with his arguing which mayby satisfy Heavy Arms on why if Gaia do not want Garouinterbreeding she even let it be possible.<br /> Metis are nothing for a longtime solution. But they exist if shit hit the fan and you need a short time solution in getting asap more Garou to fight a problem. So Metis are deformed and steril because Gaia do not want Garou to only breed with themselves and so over long time make them extinct because of to much interbreeding but they are possible if you lost many Garou and need soon many fighters and because you expect the losses would be high it is not so a big thing if they are steril when they will die anyway. So Metis are the emergency option if Garou need to make an army to turn back the scales to the favour of Gaia and with how dire the situation is now and there are so many hearings about septs breeding metis to have the fighters to turn back the Wyrm he thinks that right now is the situation for Metisbreeding not be forbidden but encouraged to tip the balance back to Gaia.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-16T08:05:43-07:00","id":1403100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1403059#post1403059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I remember som 20 years ago, when we all were early twenties, a lot of female players in the LARP had their characters have lupus babies between games. Back then the revised rule that cubs always have the mothers breed wasn't enforced in the game and we went with the offspring has the breed of the non-changer parent (which makes more sense in my mind).<br /> <br /> Anyways, as the players grew older, and had real-life babies, this ceased. It wasn't the most rewarding game element anyways.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I freaking WISH that was what I was talking about. I truly do. But no, I'm referring to the rather disturbing tendencity for people to pop in WtA forums and declare that the lupus breed is <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">dog rape</div></div> </div> </div> and refuse to budge.<br /> <br /> Then Changing Ways goes out of its freaking way to encourage this view.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-16T09:08:11-07:00","id":1403104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Koronus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1403083#post1403083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it is a mixture from Garou choosing themselves to treat Metis badly, tribechieftains only trying to listen to exact words and not the spirit like Dschingis Khan is saying, that the apocalypse seems to be 5 before twelve and that so many homids comming from a times where equality and romantic is treated with high value.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, probably all contributing factors.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Koronus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1403083#post1403083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Metis are nothing for a longtime solution. But they exist if shit hit the fan and you need a short time solution in getting asap more Garou to fight a problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>The idea has a presumption, that aren't necessarly true:<br /> Gaia has had any intention or purpouse in mind, when creating Metis. She didn't need to. It could be, that the deformity of the Metis is just there, with no reason or intend behind it.<br /> 'Guaridians of the Caerns' has one legend about first Metis and iirc, the Metis deformity was as much a shortsighted reaction of Gaia to the Breach of the Litany, as the Breach itself was a emotion driven laps of judgement (I mean a Strider and a Child of Gaia meet at the place of slaughter where a War of Rage era summit ended badly and have grief driven sex - not mentally healthy or is it?).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-16T09:19:09-07:00","id":1403105,"title":"","content":"<br /> societies have historically not-used some of it's populace for racial or other prejudices in wars. For example Black Americans were excluded from fighting with white americans during WWII (when they did fight, they were segregated units) <br /> <br /> The thing is, if you are cruel to metis, you are discouraging other Garou from having metis, because such Garou don't want to have miserable children. Garou prejudice makes sense, it's not right, but it makes sense. you are sacrificing the individual for the sake of the group.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-16T10:37:26-07:00","id":1403113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Koronus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1403083#post1403083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> So Metis are deformed and steril because Gaia do not want Garou to only breed with themselves and so over long time make them extinct because of to much interbreeding but they are possible if you lost many Garou and need soon many fighters and because you expect the losses would be high it is not so a big thing if they are steril when they will die anyway. So Metis are the emergency option if Garou need to make an army to turn back the scales to the favour of Gaia and with how dire the situation is now and there are so many hearings about septs breeding metis to have the fighters to turn back the Wyrm he thinks that right now is the situation for Metisbreeding not be forbidden but encouraged to tip the balance back to Gaia.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, the Changing Ways -itself- notes, metis births are -insanely- costly for the sept with very little reward and a lot of gambling.<br /> <br /> First off, each metis pregnancy can end with the mother dead. That is one warrior less. Second, raising a metis to fighting age takes 10 years. Third, you will never know the deformities the metis has, they are like a 9 month kinder egg that might have unusable deformities for a shock troop.<br /> <br /> What we here have seen as a MUCH less risky (though no more morally solid) method of cheap troops is this;<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> Get a bunch of high content wolf-dogs. Breed them in lupus form. The pregnancy lasts 2 months, and garou gene is decided 1/10 per -pup.- So the more pups, the more potential garou you have. Any non-garou pups are still kin and can be bred for more tries for garou. Best part? Lupus shift at 2-3 years old. So for every metis cub, you could have 10+ lupus ready. </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> A single metis cub is a HUGE drain on resources of a sept, taxing a bunch of garou who have better things to do. For 10 years and with a very likely death of the mother.<br /> <br /> Basically, Changing Ways' shock Troop metis idea is very much not canon-compliant.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-16T11:06:22-07:00","id":1403123,"title":"","content":"Then it seems the Book contradict itself because in the same book I read that many septs in Wyrmplagued regions start breeding Metis to get the situation back under controle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-16T12:30:58-07:00","id":1403143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Koronus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1403123#post1403123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then it seems the Book contradict itself because in the same book I read that many septs in Wyrmplagued regions start breeding Metis to get the situation back under controle.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, it does. It starts the metis section by being VERY clear how dangerous a birth of a metis is. And ends it with BSD level metis production. Something BSDs can do due to higher numbers+centuries of planning+having other sources of garou.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I just want to note that as much as I am speaking bad of Changing Ways, this is due to the book being inconsistent more than me hating it.<br /> <br /> As for the thread topic, as Heavy Arms so well put it; Metis as a whole punch down with religious justification. As much as it is pointed out that the abuse IS unearned, there are still a lot of things that do speak of them being wrong due to disability and origin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":110,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","user":"Ana Mizuki","date":". 07-16-2020, 08:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-17T06:10:11-07:00","id":1403216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Koronus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1403123#post1403123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then it seems the Book contradict itself because in the same book I read that many septs in Wyrmplagued regions start breeding Metis to get the situation back under controle.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but they are living in Wyrmplagued regions - only there they would get twisted ideas like breaking a tenet of the litany on purpouse to breed children to sacrifice them in 10 years.<br /> I mean even the basic idea is grotesque.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-18T01:45:19-07:00","id":1403355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1403143#post1403143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yep, it does. It starts the metis section by being VERY clear how dangerous a birth of a metis is. And ends it with BSD level metis production. Something BSDs can do due to higher numbers+centuries of planning+having other sources of garou.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I just want to note that as much as I am speaking bad of Changing Ways, this is due to the book being inconsistent more than me hating it.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Bear in mind Changing Ways was greatly altered during the approvals process and a lot of the stupider contents were added by White Wolf/Paradox after the manuscript was completed against the Developers wishes. I suspect the 'BSD level metis production' is one of those additions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-18T09:02:34-07:00","id":1403393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1403355#post1403355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Bear in mind Changing Ways was greatly altered during the approvals process and a lot of the stupider contents were added by White Wolf/Paradox after the manuscript was completed against the Developers wishes. I suspect the 'BSD level metis production' is one of those additions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, I was one of the first to read the book. It legit does seem like the 'shocking' elements were added MUCH later in the writing.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-07T16:28:56-07:00","id":1406856,"title":"","content":"Caveat, I have not read this thread.<br /> <br /> I have some disabilities, though of course that in no way &quot;authorizes&quot; me to speak for anyone else with disabilities, let alone ones I don't have.<br /> <br /> I don't think Metis should be removed from W5 (although given the rumor that <b>stepping sideways</b> is being removed, I may not care at all about W5). I don't mind Metis but I do hate retcons. W5 as a continuation of the metaplot into the 2010's and 2020's is useless if all prior history is retconned. Guess what, Metis are part of that prior history. It would be just as disruptive as retconning away the Lupus, or the Gurahl or the Bastet.<br /> <br /> I do think their name and depiction should change. Yes, the Garou would give them a disparaging name, but that doesn't have to be an OOC slap in the face of a Native American nation, too. And why would the Bastet call Metis by a disparaging name? They don't see anything wrong with Metis, and barely even punish the parents. Bastet Metis get the coolest Gifts, and nobody can steal them. Ajaba no longer care what Breed a werehyena is, although maybe in the past they did. And like the Dalit, maybe Garou Metis have their own name for themselves now.<br /> <br /> Something very important to understand about disability is that being disabled is not inherent to any particular body or brain arrangement. A very short human is only disabled if they live in a society of people who are all taller than them. I, standing 5'4&quot;, would be profoundly disabled in a hobbit society just because I wouldn't fit indoors. A tailless Garou does not communicate in the same exact way that other Garou communicate, but that is only a disadvantage if other Garou are unwilling or unable to meet them halfway. A two-tailed Garou doesn't even communicate differently from their septmates. My hypersensitivity to stereos and construction vehicle noise wouldn't matter in the slightest if I lived in a quiet, pre-industrial farming village - in fact, I wouldn't even be aware I was &quot;disabled&quot; if I lived in a quieter society. In a zero-G space station, having usable legs would barely matter. In Africa, albinism is a death sentence both because of horrible skin cancer, and because some people hunt albinos for sport. In the U.S., albinism mostly just means you need to be careful of your eyes in direct sunlight. People with Autism are viewed as incapable of functioning in human society -- because every society is made by and for people without Autism. If Autistic people were the majority, I guarantee you that the non-Autistic folks would be at a profound disadvantage for all the mental feats which come easily to those with Autism and are very difficult for those without Autism. A Metis with three eyes or two tails is just odd-looking, and unable to blend into human or wolf society - they have no actual physical disadvantage. Having no fur doesn't really matter much if you live in a hot climate and are immune to diseases spread by bloodsucking parasites.<br /> <br /> Every single person has things they're good at, and things they're not good at. Whether the latter count as &quot;disabilities&quot; is based on what their society and environment expect or demand of them, not on some inherent inferiority. This is also a truth in evolution within any species: traits that are advantages in one environment can become maladaptive when circumstances change, and must be replaced with new adaptations for the species to keep thriving.<br /> <br /> As a disabled person, I grew up thinking of myself as a freak because of the way I am treated by most self-proclaimed &quot;normal&quot; humans. Then I grew up and realised there's nothing whatsoever &quot;wrong&quot; with me. ALL the problems I have in life are caused by discrimination rather than my &quot;disability&quot;. I'm not &quot;damaged&quot; and my differences don't feel like a &quot;curse&quot; from God. The only people punishing me are mortal bigots. My &quot;disabilities&quot; give me amazing abilities that &quot;normal&quot; people don't have -- but they aren't advantages because &quot;normal&quot; people don't value or reward those abilities.<br /> <br /> I don't know how to translate this into mechanics, other than ensuring that the three Breeds are mechanically balanced. But it can certainly be conveyed in the writing (and is already in some Werewolf writing). It isn't disparaging to depict Garou contempt for the disabled because that contempt is a constant reality for real disabled people. It is, unfortunately, part of being disabled. It would only be unintentionally disparaging if the voices and accomplishments of Metis characters somehow disappeared from W5. I don't think any of the Metis deformities published so far make a character unplayable or unable to fight for Gaia, not even the lack of claws or weak immune system.<br /> <br /> <br /> I have my own theory for the nature and origin of the Metis in this setting, based partly on in-character opinions I read in Guardians of the Caerns, partly on the different outcomes of &quot;inbreeding&quot; in other Changing-Breeds, and partly on somebody's suggestion that if the shapeshifters didn't depend on their Kinfolk for breeding, they would have wiped out humanity and/or let their animal kin go extinct. I think that Gaia (or Luna and Helios) made every Changing-Breed dependent on their Kinfolk for breeding, not to prevent Metis from existing but to remind the shapeshifters that their Kinfolk are valuable. Perhaps the shapeshifters were created for the sake of the humans and animals, not the other way around? Gaia accomplishes this in different ways with different Changing-Breeds, though. Some have no conception, or a stillbirth, if two shifters breed. The Grondr had sterile, but non-deformed &quot;Metis&quot;, who were an entire Auspice and necessary for the wereboars to do their duties. The Nagah have non-deformed, fertile Ahi, but a female Nagah can only birth one Ahi in her whole life. The Kitsune have fertile, non-deformed Shinju children, but normally one of the Kitsune parents dies at the child's birth.<br /> <br /> So Gaia (or Luna and Helios) told most shapeshifters not to inbreed. Then some Changing-Breeds (Garou, Bastet, Ajaba, Ratkin) either screwed each other for the very first time... or started making a habit of it. And I think the Metis were born as a result. Not as a &quot;punishment&quot; but as a warning. They're sterile because otherwise Kinfolk would no longer matter. But why are they &quot;deformed&quot;? There are possible explanations that don't require deformity to be the inherently bad thing most Garou think it is: <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Metis have two shifter parents, so they're &quot;closer&quot; to Gaia. Thus, Gaia's pain or injuries are written on their bodies in some way. This is only as &quot;bad&quot; and dishonorable as a battle scar. Maybe originally, the Metis weren't deformed, merely sterile. Maybe in previous ages, the deformities were more obviously not actually disadvantages, merely neutral differences.</li> <li>The Garou slaughtered the other children of Gaia because they served Her in a different way from the Garou, and they could not tolerate a different way of living. They still fight each other over Tribal differences. The Metis are there to remind or teach the Garou that even someone who is &quot;different&quot; from you is still Gaia's child and chosen. Until the Garou learn to accept their own dang children as equals, they won't learn to accept the other Changing-Breeds. This goes for the Bastet, Ajaba, and Ratkin too, who have plenty of racist attitudes themselves.</li> <li>The Metis are closer to Gaia, and/or created to help fix new problems that have arisen. They have to pay a price of <i>some</i> kind for their amazing kickass Gifts, otherwise they'd take over and shapeshifter societies would become unbalanced. So far, only the Bastet Metis have the kind of Gifts everyone else envies, but that could be changed. Ajaba Metis also have a uniquely useful position in their Breed's society, as the middle between the extreme personalities of males and females.</li> </ol><br /> I do think it would help to make spontaneous metis clearly different from real metis. There is a problem with the message that &quot;wrong&quot; breeding, and/or disability, is being associated with pollution and radiation poisoning. Even though pollution and radiation poisoning can cause physical birth &quot;defects&quot;, this isn't a message I like to see.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 08-07-2020, 08:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-08T13:47:00-07:00","id":1407023,"title":"","content":"Metis is from the greek god, not the native americans. Next book should really, really clarify that. <br /> <br /> <br /> I really don't think the &quot;World of <b><i>Darkness</i></b>&quot; should be body positive, at least not on the surface. Everything should be more shit than it is, but it should make you realise what's actually shit, and the way Garou treat metis should make people think 'wow that's pretty shitty, I won't do that in real life/I will fight against that in real life'. The book absolutely should not tell you what's shit, but show you what's shit (V5 really dropped the ball there). The Metis may be debilitated, and there might be some kinda-reasonable ideas behind metis hatred (when done publicly, to some extent it discourages potential future metis parents) but the players should understand that metis getting the shitter is wrong (even if their characters don't) <br /> <br /> Honestly, I think Metis problems should include some really controversial stuff; Diabetes, uncontrollable Obesity, gender dysphoria,developmental disorders, down syndrome... I understand some tables might not want this and some players really shouldn't , but if done right, it could be really good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-09T04:02:48-07:00","id":1407110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1407023#post1407023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Metis is from the greek god, not the native americans. Next book should really, really clarify that.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the next book goes here, it needs to be straight up and honest about it. Metis weren't named after the Greek goddess. They were named after the French word for &quot;mixed,&quot; and at best by people that didn't realize it was used for the distinct cultural group of mixed ethnicity Native and European descendants.<br /> <br /> If they want to keep the name, but recontextualize it's origins, they have to be open about it in a side-bar or something. Just making it sound like it was always meant to be about a Greek mythological figure is a bad look.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I really don't think the &quot;World of <b><i>Darkness</i></b>&quot; should be body positive, at least not on the surface. </div> </div> </div>We have Pentex for this. As was discussed earlier, the narrative needs to punch up. All the Pentex subsidiaries pushing toxic body image advertising to sell you their products are things for the narrative to punch up on by highlighting the ills of such industries that know exactly what sort of psychological tools they're using for profit while not caring about the damage it does to people that can never live up to such messaging.<br /> <br /> The WoD isn't body positive. It's a world where people pay for the most effective cosmetics, drugs, and surgeries to look like marketing tells them to; blind to the literal rotting of their souls they're purchasing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...the way Garou treat metis should make people think 'wow that's pretty shitty, I won't do that in real life/I will fight against that in real life'. The book absolutely should not tell you what's shit, but show you what's shit (V5 really dropped the ball there). The Metis may be debilitated, and there might be some kinda-reasonable ideas behind metis hatred (when done publicly, to some extent it discourages potential future metis parents) but the players should understand that metis getting the shitter is wrong (even if their characters don't) </div> </div> </div>And the current Metis narrative doesn't work to get here. It doesn't prompt you to think about how people with socially shunned body types are treated, because it blames those things on the &quot;good&quot; higher powers.<br /> <br /> If you wanted to highlight police brutality against PoC in the US in a WoD game, you can't put in a rule that says that PoC fly into a deadly rage when confronted by authority figures. The message of needing a better world where police need to focus on harm reduction and deescalation, and municipalities need to spend more money on response services that aren't armed for non-violent situations so armed cops don't need to respond to everything, is lost when your fictional world makes it so not being ready to use lethal force instantly in situations involving PoC is actually stupid.<br /> <br /> And that's the problem with the Metis as is. The case of needing to treat them poorly is too strong to promote actual empathy. The discrimination against them is a necessary evil people agree with more than a broken system that people see a need to overthrow for something better.<br /> <br /> The &quot;progressive&quot; wing of the Garou Nation (beyond the most extreme radicals on the verge of being made Ronin) are fighting for treating Metis better, not treating them equally.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Honestly, I think Metis problems should include some really controversial stuff; Diabetes, uncontrollable Obesity, gender dysphoria,developmental disorders, down syndrome... I understand some tables might not want this and some players really shouldn't , but if done right, it could be really good. </div> </div> </div>The number of times these things would be used poorly (like plenty of the existing ones already have been) and caused negative experiences for people vastly outweigh the value of the few times people would get it right.<br /> <br /> Beyond that, a lot of these have significant issues in the real of playability. A Garou with untreated diabetes is going to be practically unplayable since managing a purely diet/activity regimen isn't really compatible with being a warrior of Gaia. If they can take medication, it's practically a non-issue outside of extremely narrow circumstances.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-09T04:29:06-07:00","id":1407114,"title":"","content":"in that case<br /> 'we garou used the word metis before it became racist'<br /> <br /> re diabetes: Does it not come with other issues even with insulin injection? The one guy i remember with t1 seemed pretty healthy, but really tried to achieve that. but the guys I know with t2... Granted, they literally brought it on themselves, but it seems to come with a lot of issues not readily identifiable as an issue with blood sugar. The garou being physically intensive as they are might either mitigate or agravate these secondary effects... but i acknowledge my knowledge on the subject is lacking: still, magical curse ilness doesn't neccessarily need to perfectly mirror reality. <br /> <br /> at the least, needing rite of binding for insulin, and having difficulties with long missions, could be significant enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 08-09-2020, 07:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-09T07:17:43-07:00","id":1407133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1407114#post1407114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">in that case<br /> 'we garou used the word metis before it became racist'</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not an in-character problem (beyond the Garou lexicon being immersion breakingly nonsensical), it's a game-writing problem.<br /> <br /> The Garou can be written to use any word they want. Hell, they should really just call the Breed Crinos, since the other two Breeds are named after the form they're born in. If it was that way from the beginning we'd have never noticed it.<br /> <br /> If there was a Tribal camp called the [Slur] Lynchers, it wouldn't matter that they've called themselves that for 5,000 years in-universe. A game being written today (or in the early 90s) should have come up with a different name, even if somehow the naming was an accident because it means something else in another language (which is super easy to do). <br /> <br /> Esp. for W5, there's no impetus to avoid change like there was for W20. While lots of us have issues with some of the name changes in V5, there's still plenty that were a long time coming.<br /> <br /> If they're going to keep using Metis, there need to put a rock solid reason in the books that speaks from the authors to the readers on why they felt it was important vs. picking a less problematic word for the splat. They don't need to come up with in-universe reasons on how the word started getting used that way for the characters.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Does it not come with other issues even with insulin injection? </div> </div> </div>It can, as noted there are different types of the disease, but in general both major types of diabetes can be controlled with medication and lifestyle to have minimal impact on daily life. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> at the least, needing rite of binding for insulin, and having difficulties with long missions, could be significant enough. </div> </div> </div>Well, really, what this boils down to is that you'd have to join the Bone Gnawers or Glass Walkers for your Renown to survive it, and get your hands on a specific Fetish that would let you carry around lots of your meds for you where either your or someone you know did the Rites on to make sure they're work on Garou. Having a months supply or so (depending on individual dosing and so on) really wouldn't be hard, and more than that is actually harder because insulin doesn't have a long shelf life so after a month it would start going bad. So you might not be an Umbral explorer, but you can get some decently long missions in even away from civilization.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> magical curse ilness doesn't neccessarily need to perfectly mirror reality. </div> </div> </div>Moved this out to the end to keep the points more coherent. This statement is a perfect reason for Metis deformities to not be real world disorders and focus on the more supernatural ones. We don't need magical-rules-diabetes for Metis to suffer.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-09T07:20:24-07:00","id":1407134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1407110#post1407110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> We have Pentex for this. As was discussed earlier, the narrative needs to punch up. All the Pentex subsidiaries pushing toxic body image advertising to sell you their products are things for the narrative to punch up on by highlighting the ills of such industries that know exactly what sort of psychological tools they're using for profit while not caring about the damage it does to people that can never live up to such messaging.<br /> <br /> The WoD isn't body positive. It's a world where people pay for the most effective cosmetics, drugs, and surgeries to look like marketing tells them to; blind to the literal rotting of their souls they're purchasing.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think that in W5 Pentex should be depicted as truly insidious. Pentex should promote any kind of body positivity, supporting modern day activism against fat shaming and similar, and at the same time, promoting gym-culture and so on. Pentex is a tentacular thing, that is extremely good and exceptional at using marketing, moral codes and activism in order to manipulate any kind of mass and/or culture, trying to be the good guy, and truth is, that a well done and dangerous villain is the one that persuade the world to see him as the good guy.<br /> Pentex should penetrate almost every kind of lifestyle, activism, hobby and so on. Tainted and dangerous food, anabolic substances, drugs, brainwashing through massive advertising on social network and tv about politics and social stuff, but at the same time financing mercyless capitalism, right, left, whatever, in order to corrupt corrupt corrupt and corrupt in every form, everywhere, without any kind of humanity or mercy, showing how much Pentex could corrupt people even without using demonic powers, pulling out greed, envy and hate from everyone.<br /> <br /> <br /> At the same time, I think that some tribes based on some kind of extreme warrior culture, should be really hardcore on their standard about bodies and fighting capabilities. A warrior is not raised with kindness and tolerance.<br /> <br /> Progress/tradition is one of the pillar of werewolf, but what happen when the youngster want to promote a ''traditional'' rebellion against the elder, exactly when the elders decide that is time to progress because tradition almost killed Gaia?<br /> <br /> Tragedy is the key. Pentex is the unstoppable monster that can manipulate everything you fight for, everything you trust, everything you think is good. Is the black void the can devour your emotions and rip off any kind of hope from the garou.<br /> <br /> <br /> Just my two cents.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-09T14:43:05-07:00","id":1407187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Helur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1407134#post1407134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that in W5 Pentex should be depicted as truly insidious.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again though, you need to be careful with the political message here. If Pentex is equally pervasive in all aspects of modern life, you're painting people truly fighting for a better world as corrupt as those happily profiting from whatever actions provide them with the greatest personal returns.<br /> <br /> Which isn't to say Pentex shouldn't be selling some of its brands as &quot;woke&quot; or whatever, but this should be done as a critique of corporate pandering rather than successful subversion of positive causes. It might be the WoD, but you need to give the players something to fight for, not make the world so bleak there's no point because everything is already so tainted that the game makes itself pointless.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> At the same time, I think that some tribes based on some kind of extreme warrior culture, should be really hardcore on their standard about bodies and fighting capabilities. A warrior is not raised with kindness and tolerance. </div> </div> </div>I mean, there isn't actually any Tribe this extreme. The Fenrir are the closest, but even they know that being a warrior society means more than just being the best hand-to-hand fighters and they need Garou with different specializations to truly be effective. A scout and spy that makes sure the main line warriors know where the enemy is, and can advise their leaders on the best way to organize their forces, aren't going to look like the Garou you send to rip the enemy to shreds with claws. Etc.<br /> <br /> The Garou aren't about producing the best warrior on the planet, but about being warriors executing a global war. Which means diversity is a vital factor that human warrior cultures have actually embraced for thousands of years.<br /> <br /> [quoote]Pentex is the unstoppable monster that can manipulate everything you fight for, everything you trust, everything you think is good. Is the black void the can devour your emotions and rip off any kind of hope from the garou.[/QUOTE]<br /> <br /> Putting all the antagonist functions in the game on Pentex probably isn't a great way to handle things. Pentex is a corporation for a reason, it's not the Wyrm itself","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-09T22:06:26-07:00","id":1407233,"title":"","content":"One of the things that should be remembered when discussing how allowing WoD is or how progressive it is, is whether we are talking about the in-universe lore OR the message the mechanics and rules give us.<br /> <br /> The former can be as flawed as it wants to be, but the latter cannot be like that. Which is the issue brought up by metis/anything that discusses minority rights. Which is why it is important to think on what things like naming the inbred disabled breed 'metis' say to the player.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-10T02:13:18-07:00","id":1407251,"title":"","content":"It is hard to control how much readers interpret into something. Sure, whoever coined the term Metis for WtA might not have put that much thought into it and how it might be perceived, or maybe he or she did and came to other conclusions than we do today. It would require some level of suspension of disbelieve to acknowledge that terms like Philodox, Ragabash and Metis and what not are just terms of an fictional language without relation to human languages of any sort.<br /> <br /> For all we know, the term was created by pulling random letters form a bag of Scrabble stones. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-10T04:02:44-07:00","id":1407261,"title":"","content":"Honestly the 'Metis' being a french word for half natives in canada? <br /> <br /> Totally overblown non-issue. If I met an 'actual' metis north America I'm fairly certain I won't confuse him or her with an inbred werewolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-10T04:14:36-07:00","id":1407264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1407251#post1407251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is hard to control how much readers interpret into something.</div> </div> </div> </div>And there's no reason here to let perfect by the enemy of good.<br /> <br /> Just because it's hard to control, doesn't mean the writers of W5 shouldn't try to do better; esp. for such a long standing and well known issue.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It would require some level of suspension of disbelieve to acknowledge that terms like Philodox, Ragabash and Metis and what not are just terms of an fictional language without relation to human languages of any sort. </div> </div> </div>Given the WtA creators decided to use real words for the most part (with a scant few exceptions) - even if many archaic or using alternate spellings - and established that the in-universe Garou lexicon is something that was actively created (credited to the Fianna, which actually explains it being mostly dominated by rare English words with influences from Greek, Latin, and French), it's pretty hard to believe there was an intention we'd have to actually suspend disbelief. Outside of made a short lived attempt to claim the Garou came up with the words first in a few cases.<br /> <br /> The earlier WoD writers actually did a decide job in most cases of coming up with jargon that aids the suspension of disbelief as it turns out that immortals and various past-obsessed supernatural critters tend to use old words that aren't part of common vernaculars any more. Metis isn't even a problem in this regard; it's just not good for the exact reason Ana Mizuki noted.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-10T04:18:57-07:00","id":1407267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1407261#post1407261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I met an 'actual' metis north America I'm fairly certain I won't confuse him or her with an inbred werewolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, what do you think would happen if you met a Metis person and told them that you loved a game where Metis is a term for characters born deformed because their parents had sex when they weren't supposed to according to religious taboos?<br /> <br /> Do you think they'd go, &quot;Awesome, I want to play this game, tell me more!&quot; or try as politely as possible to end the conversation to get away from having to deal with casual racism in games?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-10T04:25:40-07:00","id":1407269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1407187#post1407187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Again though, you need to be careful with the political message here. If Pentex is equally pervasive in all aspects of modern life, you're painting people truly fighting for a better world as corrupt as those happily profiting from whatever actions provide them with the greatest personal returns.<br /> <br /> Which isn't to say Pentex shouldn't be selling some of its brands as &amp;quot;woke&amp;quot; or whatever, but this should be done as a critique of corporate pandering rather than successful subversion of positive causes. It might be the WoD, but you need to give the players something to fight for, not make the world so bleak there's no point because everything is already so tainted that the game makes itself pointless.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I mean, there isn't actually any Tribe this extreme. The Fenrir are the closest, but even they know that being a warrior society means more than just being the best hand-to-hand fighters and they need Garou with different specializations to truly be effective. A scout and spy that makes sure the main line warriors know where the enemy is, and can advise their leaders on the best way to organize their forces, aren't going to look like the Garou you send to rip the enemy to shreds with claws. Etc.<br /> <br /> The Garou aren't about producing the best warrior on the planet, but about being warriors executing a global war. Which means diversity is a vital factor that human warrior cultures have actually embraced for thousands of years.<br /> <br /> [quoote]Pentex is the unstoppable monster that can manipulate everything you fight for, everything you trust, everything you think is good. Is the black void the can devour your emotions and rip off any kind of hope from the garou.</div> </div> </div> </div>Putting all the antagonist functions in the game on Pentex probably isn't a great way to handle things. Pentex is a corporation for a reason, it's not the Wyrm itself[/QUOTE]<br /> <br /> Your point on pentex doesnt necessary exclude my point. It s really up also to the storyteller and the players. We at my table always enjoy the world of darkness with almost everything rotten from within and Pentex is perfect to penetrate any kind of human activity because its the kind of villain that must seduce you to buy , consume and trust the brand , and as brand , it must support the most positive and human things of the world , from activism to politics if the direction manages to do It. As a megacorporation a lot of people will oppose Pentex , and thats why they will try to corrupt in some other insidious ways, making you think that you are truly changing the world, that you are winning because even them are supporting you.<br /> The difference , in my chronicles, is always made by pc and npc, even bad ones that will find a way to redeem themselves from some kind of extreme behaviours inherited by their tribe or attitude. The true win , for us , is to see the Players garou to have little but epic victories in order to make people see the world as It truly is, including pentex and its machinations. <br /> But again , I think its also a matter of taste.<br /> <br /> About the warrior thing I agree with you but werewolf often has romanticized a lot this thing. To be' able to oppose such enemies as the wyrm, a warrior culture must adapt but at the same time it needs a great intolerance for failure and defeat , especially for some tribes like the lords or the fenris. I Never depict the fenris as &quot;common&quot; people , their culture is based on glorious achievements and mighty in battle, this alone can't make them really tolerant or prone to accept low standards regarding physical culture. Especially now, with Gaia almost dead and a homeless war. If I watch the news and open some links about global warming, political tension, pollution and corruption , I cant immagine the garou like in the 90'. They should be' extremely angry and ready to push themselves very far away from the edge. <br /> <br /> Again , all of this is also matter of personal taste and experience. Im not saying werewolf should be as I wrote , but that would be' how I will Play 5 edition , in a way or another.<br /> <br /> As I said , in wta we always enjoyed tragedy and a true hopeless struggle in order to give Life to a spark of hope that can become fire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-10T05:02:56-07:00","id":1407273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1407267#post1407267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, what do you think would happen if you met a Metis person and told them that you loved a game where Metis is a term for characters born deformed because their parents had sex when they weren't supposed to according to religious taboos?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd question what circumstances contrived me to say something so stupid? I enjoy risky conversations; I have in the past entertained my italian friends with WWII italian history, and we all laughed at the fascists together. But there's nothing really entertaining about bringing that up. If anything, from what I'm reading, the Term Metis today has a different usage from what it had a hundred or so years ago. Metis people refer to themselves as metis, even though it's origins come from the a derogatory term of half-breed. The meaning now is not the same as the meaning before. Imagine we really tried to avoid the use of the word 'bastard' to avoid offending children born out of wedlock? That was a pretty heavy word back in the day. If I had a Metis player at my table, I'd simply explain the context. (I don't think I even pronounce it the same.) and if they really didn't like it, I'd call em something else; maybe bastards, or would that offend too many?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-10T05:36:19-07:00","id":1407278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1407261#post1407261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly the 'Metis' being a french word for half natives in canada?<br /> <br /> Totally overblown non-issue. If I met an 'actual' metis north America I'm fairly certain I won't confuse him or her with an inbred werewolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>In an American game with not one but TWO tribes who are outright said to be Native American? In a game that very much tries to be inclusive to all kinds of players?<br /> <br /> The issue is not what a white American/European person might think on it, it is that if a First Nations/Native American person picks up the game and see their tribe name in such a context. And what does it say about the writing if we are not considering them as part of the player-base?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-10T06:34:40-07:00","id":1407286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Helur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1407269#post1407269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Im not saying werewolf should be as I wrote , but that would be' how I will Play 5 edition , in a way or another.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's worth considering that when people are talking about how the books should be written, how you plan on playing the game anyway can come off in a number of less than productive ways.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1407273#post1407273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd question what circumstances contrived me to say something so stupid?</div> </div> </div> </div>OK...that part where you acknowledge it's stupid?<br /> <br /> That's what the books ask every Metis person that picks them up. That's why lots of us have spent decades advocating it get changed in some fashion. You're calling it an overblown non-issue because it doesn't make you put down the book and dismiss WtA in disgust. I actually lost players with Native backgrounds from an online Mage game just by mentioning I was a WtA fan in the late 90s.<br /> <br /> Dealing with the name better doesn't hurt you or me, and means more people will play the game. That's what it's a real issue for us to push for. Because we want people to play the games we love with us. Not dealing with it just means there's less WtA players out there.<br /> <br /> Seems like a simple choice to me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Metis people refer to themselves as metis, even though it's origins come from the a derogatory term of half-breed. </div> </div> </div>Even if the use of the word had a completely neutral history in European-Native relations in North American history, naming the Breed Metis isn't something.<br /> <br /> If there's a WtA supplement that details Pentex's premiere banking law firm is named Zimmerman, Orstein, and Goldberg, I could entertain in my mind it was an innocent mistake. I would also treat any push back against changing it over how obnoxiously anti-Semitic it is poorly. I do appreciate the some people might need the dots connected for them because they're not steeped in anti-Semitic jargon, but if WW back in the 90s had that in the books, and refused to get rid of it, I'd probably have never even gotten into their games at all as WtA 2e was the second book from the company I read and the first I bought.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Imagine we really tried to avoid the use of the word 'bastard' to avoid offending children born out of wedlock? </div> </div> </div>Um, I wouldn't use it around a kid that met the dictionary definition even as society is changing to be far more accepting of decoupling marriage and having children. I'd probably use it in informal situations in front of adults born out of wedlock because I'd be less conscious of my word choice, but I'd absolutely not use it casually if I knew it was upsetting to someone in the social group. Mostly because it is a much milder word to use than it used to be. <br /> <br /> If I was writing a TTRPG, I'd definitely consider it a word to avoid using unless I felt it was sufficiently appropriate to the context of what I was writing, even then use it sparingly, and most certainly avoid making it the name of something if I could avoid it (obviously if I was writing The Inglourious Basterds RPG it would be hard to avoid a lot of things I might otherwise).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-10T09:36:16-07:00","id":1407314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1407023#post1407023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Metis is from the greek god, not the native americans. Next book should really, really clarify that. <br /> <br /> <br /> I really don't think the &amp;quot;World of <b><i>Darkness</i></b>&amp;quot; should be body positive, at least not on the surface. Everything should be more shit than it is, but it should make you realise what's actually shit, and the way Garou treat metis should make people think 'wow that's pretty shitty, I won't do that in real life/I will fight against that in real life'. The book absolutely should not tell you what's shit, but show you what's shit (V5 really dropped the ball there). The Metis may be debilitated, and there might be some kinda-reasonable ideas behind metis hatred (when done publicly, to some extent it discourages potential future metis parents) but the players should understand that metis getting the shitter is wrong (even if their characters don't) <br /> <br /> Honestly, I think Metis problems should include some really controversial stuff; Diabetes, uncontrollable Obesity, gender dysphoria,developmental disorders, down syndrome... I understand some tables might not want this and some players really shouldn't , but if done right, it could be really good.</div> </div> </div> </div>M\u00e9tis have nothing to do with their creation, they are literally getting punished for the sins of their parents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-10T11:05:53-07:00","id":1407329,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25794_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25794\" data-vbnamecard=\"25794\">MyWifeIsScary</a> just because &quot;metis&quot; as a name for the deformed, hated offspring of miscegenation doesn't dehumanize your family or aggressively throw centuries of racist violence against your family into your face, doesn't mean that it's OK for the game to be written to do that to other people. Writers who are happy to shit upon and dehumanize people of color are BAD writers, no matter what crappy excuse they come up with.<br /> <br /> Do you have any idea what it's like to grow up in a society that tells you, every single day, that you are a subhuman POS and you shouldn't exist, that merely allowing you to eat is a privilege you shouldn't take for granted? Do you have any idea how that nonstop hatred and verbal abuse tortures a person's psyche? How easy it is for that to truly break someone? My guess is you don't, or you wouldn't advocate keeping a pointless racial slur in the game just because it doesn't hurt <i>you</i> personally.<br /> <br /> The word 'metis' is not in any way necessary for the theme or mood of Werewolf. Keeping it accomplishes nothing except advertise that this is a racist game for whites only. In 1E it was an honest mistake, but there is no possible justification for keeping it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 08-10-2020, 02:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-10T11:09:52-07:00","id":1407332,"title":"","content":"The World of Darkness is a satirical setting: <br /> Thus it becomes intellectually dishonest to write a setting where people only &quot;punch up&quot;. The real art would be to present a setting where people kick down so hard they injure their foot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-10T11:36:00-07:00","id":1407338,"title":"","content":"The narrative of the game should punch-up, even if the setting punches down (especially if the setting punches down) because the game is punk by its nature and punk is punching up.<br /> <br /> The game itself however, not the setting, should NOT be punching down. The sheer fact that it\u2019s against the spirit of the game and is imo morally wrong aside, it\u2019s just not pragmatic. The benefit-cost ratio that comes with terms like \u2018M*tis\u2019 is obviously slanted towards cost. Every player of an indigenous or socially conscious background who puts the book down and dismisses it after seeing the term used the way it is (or the tribal names of the Pure Brothers) is entirely within their rights to do so and has actively lost the company a sale, particularly in the RPG market where buy-in to a franchise is so important for its success and growth.<br /> <br /> The term simply doesn\u2019t offer enough benefit to merit its inclusion imo. It was born out of a lack of understanding for the context and it\u2019s been kept out of habit. There is no reason why it couldn\u2019t be exchanged for a more irl neutral term, even an in-universe pejorative term. Calling the children of two Garou \u2018Mules\u2019 or \u2018Crinos\u2019 or \u2018Runts\u2019 or \u2018Garou-born\u2019 or \u2018Wastrels\u2019 all accomplishes the in-universe goal without using an irl term for any disadvantaged group. <br /> <br /> It costs nothing to use a different term and its actively beneficial in many regards, that\u2019s why I\u2019m always surprised (we\u2019ll not surprised anymore, but annoyed) when I see this argument reoccur.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-10T12:18:00-07:00","id":1407349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1407332#post1407332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The World of Darkness is a satirical setting:<br /> Thus it becomes intellectually dishonest to write a setting where people only &quot;punch up&quot;. The real art would be to present a setting where people kick down so hard they injure their foot.</div> </div> </div> </div>From a purely simulationist standpoint, in-universe, the WOD is indeed full of slurs and horrible people saying truly despicable things. I don't disagree with you there. If the game was purely a &quot;what-if?&quot; simulation to build the most plausible World of Darkness from initial assumptions, yes it's plausible for white Garou to casually keep using a racial slur in that way. But promoting racial slurs isn't even necessary to make the WoD an awful place. And in-universe the Bastet, Ajaba, Pure Ones, Grondr, and probably Stargazers and Silent Striders would still use completely different names, which they don't currently in canon.<br /> <br /> A game, or literature, or work of music or visual art, is more than just a private exercise in academic simulation. It's a public statement. That creates potential problems even beyond the pragmatic problem of alienating large numbers of potential players. Any society, and global human society overall, is made up of the words and statements and discourse that we say to one another, and with which we surround children. This is why I asked you if you know what it's like to be bombarded with constant messages of hate while growing up. Words <b>matter</b>. Names can absolutely break the spirits of children and adults if they are part of an oppressed group. Words alone can and do drive 10-year-old children to commit suicide. If this isn't part of your personal experience, then understandably you don't know what that's like, but please have the respect to believe other people who have lived through that. Don't invalidate other peoples' experiences just because it hasn't happened to <i>you</i> personally.<br /> <br /> Words change the world. They are our real-world Awakened Magick. Words create politics and social movements. Words teach little children to love or hate themselves and their neighbors. Words teach people that violence against each other is acceptable, or not acceptable. Words teach children who counts as a person, and who is subhuman. Words are not neutral things that exist only for private simulation. The choice of words and depictions in a game or novel or album have a real, tangible, long-lasting effect on the <b>real </b>world and the lives of real people. A popular work can leave cultural and political effects for <i>centuries or millennia</i> after it's created. Those effects are not morally neutral, and wilfully ignoring them is not OK.<br /> <br /> Writing with awareness of the power of language doesn't mean we shouldn't heap up awful things in the World of Darkness. It does mean that we should be responsible in how we use awful words and situations. To draw an analogy, rape and forced pregnancy are real and surely common in the WoD, too. Of course the BSDs engage in that, but the game makes it clear they are &quot;bad guys&quot; and their behavior is not OK. BSDs aren't meant to be played, and their behavior isn't front and center at the beginning of the book. Writing about a sept of the &quot;good guys&quot; who force all female Garou to bear at least one metis whether they want to or not, for an ostensibly justifiable cause (in Changing Ways) is not OK. Gratuitous rape scenes, rape used shallowly just for shock value, and rape jokes would also not be OK in a game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 08-10-2020, 03:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-10T13:01:19-07:00","id":1407357,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I'm not overly attached to the term (it sounds good phonetically but...)<br /> I really want to ask why the term metis was chosen in the first place? was it to draw attention to a real world culture who unjustly suffer at the hands of discrimination, or am I giving early WW to much credit? They did write the Wendigo after all. <br /> <br /> The garou aren't the good guys. They're Rage empowered tribals longing for the days they ruled the world. They aren't nice people. They fight monsters, but it's never been the case that they were not monsters themselves. Garou culture is not nice. it should not become nice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-10T13:45:21-07:00","id":1407363,"title":"","content":"I have no idea why the term was chosen, you\u2019d have to ask the WtA writers about that, although I can guess they they may have come across it researching the history of indigenous North Americans and their interactions with colonial groups over the course of post-columbian exchange history.<br /> <br /> I agree that the Garou Nation is not a nice organization. It is made up of many fucked up individuals. The Garou Nation is a hyper-traditional xenophobic theocratic militant terrorist group. Many Garou have internalized the Nation\u2019s culture since birth and use it to justify numerous atrocities, physical and social. This is part of why I love them, because as they are - they are grand tragic heroes.<br /> <br /> I agree that the garou-born, at default, should be disadvantaged because of the Garou Nation\u2019s culture and experience immense prejudice for the \u2018crime\u2019 of existing. However, you can still have this without the use of real-world term used to discriminate against a real world group, particularly when the in-universe group the term is applied to are \u201cabominations born of a sinful and forbidden union\u201d.<br /> <br /> Where I diverge from you, I believe, is that I believe that the status quo is important so as to create a contrast. The game is and always has been a game of punk and that means that the Player Characters, should they choose, are there to contrast the Nation at its worst and fight to change it into something better - something good, something not only capable of winning the War but worthy of it.<br /> <br /> Even if the Player Characters are not interested in the plight of the garou-born, in any particularly chronicle, the spirit of punk should still be there. There should be some Garou, even if just a few, standing up for their cousins. The garou-born should have advocates, amongst each other and other garou alike.<br /> <br /> They will struggle against the Nation\u2019s orthodoxy, of course they will. But that struggle, the sheer act of it, is important. The NPCs on their own may never win the final battle, because for me such a thing belongs to the domain of PCs who dedicate themselves to the cause in a campaign, but by the sheer fact that they struggle the spirit of punk lives on and that makes all the difference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-10T14:57:28-07:00","id":1407383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1407363#post1407363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Where I diverge from you, I believe, is that I believe that the status quo is important so as to create a contrast. The game is and always has been a game of punk and that means that the Player Characters, should they choose, are there to contrast the Nation at its worst and fight to change it into something better - something good, something not only capable of winning the War but worthy of it.<br /> e.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not really a divergence from me at all. That's near exact what I believe: The players have the option to try to be the light raging in the darkness. Or they can have fun clowning around as eco-fascists. <br /> <br /> The issue though, is that the darkness needs to be present. As werewolf editions have gone on, they have become sanatized, nice, kind: What battles can you have when the war is already won? There are too many authors trying to make werewolf nice because that's what they would want or maybe even because that's what their character achieved in their own games but.. Who wants a nice setting in a game about Rage? It's a selfish act of setting sabbotage to deny the struggle. I wanna get mad at stuff and hulk out.<br /> <br /> There's just something horrible about removing all the bad stuff about the Garou and making the game a sanitized, politically correct corperate product, preaching to a chior with all the power of a wet blanket.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 08-10-2020, 06:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-10T15:48:11-07:00","id":1407391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1407383#post1407383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's not really a divergence from me at all. That's near exact what I believe: The players have the option to try to be the light raging in the darkness. Or they can have fun clowning around as eco-fascists. <br /> <br /> The issue though, is that the darkness needs to be present. As werewolf editions have gone on, they have become sanatized, nice, kind: What battles can you have when the war is already won? There are too many authors trying to make werewolf nice because that's what they would want or maybe even because that's what their character achieved in their own games but.. Who wants a nice setting in a game about Rage? It's a selfish act of setting sabbotage to deny the struggle. I wanna get mad at stuff and hulk out.<br /> <br /> There's just something horrible about removing all the bad stuff about the Garou and making the game a sanitized, politically correct corperate product, preaching to a chior with all the power of a wet blanket.</div> </div> </div> </div>And here I disagree with you. Just because you are not bitching against your own kind anymore does not mean that the setting is a nice one. The fight can still be dark and dirty while you play the &quot;nice guys&quot;. What always made me smirk and is fitting here is that in the old Battlefront II (now not the Dice Battlefield one) the Rebells casually said something that translates to: &quot;Good so! Use your hate!&quot; despite hate is the dark side.<br /> My point is when you are the good guys and the heroes, incorporating what is right, the universe can still be so dirty and the enemy so overwhelming, that you want to be angry and lash out against it. It is still okay to be the rage when thinking about the planet getting destroyed. It is still okay to do a massacre against places of corruption. But please let it be for things like being unable to save an important place or the old &quot;Act or Plan?&quot; like go now and prevent something and risk it is a trap or plan right and have the knowledge, that it let the enemy time to get stronger.<br /> I find if the darkness in the Nation get less better then worse because the more infighting, the harder I find it believable how a victory would be achievable.<br /> And you talk about what to do when the war is won?<br /> This would be same like asking what to do when you reach Golconda? It should be easier but there are still things to take care of like preventing general corruption if you still continue to play after an epic battle like this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":26160,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","user":"Koronus","date":". 08-10-2020, 06:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-10T16:02:50-07:00","id":1407392,"title":"","content":"Sigh. And now the &quot;PC&quot; word has come out of the Pit, along with strawman BS, to personally attack anyone and everyone who objects to <i>deliberately promoting</i> racial slurs.<br /> <br /> Nobody has ever suggested removing everything unpleasant from the setting, or making the Garou nice. No book has ever done so (except possibly CoG Revised). Gryffon and I have repeatedly stressed that the setting should still include awful things, and the Garou doing awful stuff.<br /> <br /> But now that you've brought out the strawmen, it's clear that we can't have a respectful conversation about this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 08-10-2020, 07:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-10T17:39:58-07:00","id":1407402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1407383#post1407383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's not really a divergence from me at all. That's near exact what I believe: The players have the option to try to be the light raging in the darkness. Or they can have fun clowning around as eco-fascists.<br /> <br /> The issue though, is that the darkness needs to be present. As werewolf editions have gone on, they have become sanatized, nice, kind: What battles can you have when the war is already won?</div> </div> </div> </div>The only ones that think that they've won and become self-indulgent are the Dancers. Meanwhile, there's a giant pile of antagonists and existentially-threatening situations for most of W:tA, and it's only been growing as the years go on. W20 added in a bunch of nasty new fomori and banes, and that trend would probably continue. Maybe W5 will make a call back to the Cataclysm in SF or some other old thread of impending doom.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There are too many authors trying to make werewolf nice because that's what they would want or maybe even because that's what their character achieved in their own games but.. Who wants a nice setting in a game about Rage? It's a selfish act of setting sabbotage to deny the struggle. I wanna get mad at stuff and hulk out.<br /> <br /> There's just something horrible about removing all the bad stuff about the Garou and making the game a sanitized, politically correct corperate product, preaching to a chior with all the power of a wet blanket. </div> </div> </div>How the hell does the setting come across as nice after a read-through of W20 BotW? That could make one forget that W20 opened with the Eighth Sign of the Phoenix. But you know, even if you can work to defeat your enemies, that work doesn't just happen. It still has everything from stacked against it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-10T18:45:06-07:00","id":1407414,"title":"","content":"Maybe I\u2019m not seeing your argument, but I feel as though we\u2019re no longer arguing the same point MyWifeIsScary. <br /> <br /> I\u2019ve mentioned on this forum a few times my two general schools of thought above the kinds of game there are, Gothic style and Punk style. So I apologize if I was in accurate about our views diverging with regard to the importance of punk style gameplay.<br /> <br /> To your other points though, I was very explicitly not arguing for any sort of sanitation of the setting. My argument, and the argument of others, has been that the term \u2018m*tis\u2019 is both unnecessary and actively harmful to the game and by extension it\u2019s setting. I very clearly illustrated that I believe the setting narrative of prejudice against the Garou-born by culturally orthodox Garou is something I believe to be important and useful to the punkish nature of the setting. I also agree that solving too many problems via metaplot can cheat the players out of a chance to solve these problems themselves - that\u2019s always been a concern regarding the metaplot in general.<br /> <br /> Where you and I seem to differ is what is necessary for the game and it\u2019s themes to be effective. I don\u2019t believe that the game needs to use a slur aimed at real world groups facing discrimination to be effective. It can accomplish its narrative goals very well without using the slur which, you know, many players would not be comfortable playing with - particularly if it has ever effected them or anyone close to them personally.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ll leave the debate over \u2018political correctness\u2019 aside for now, although I will personally say that I strongly disagree with its use as a dirty phrase or criticism. <br /> <br /> What I will ultimately say is that I have been very clear about what I find objectionable and unnecessary. I don\u2019t take issue with the narrative, I take issue with the term harnessed by the narrative, because it is harmful to the effectiveness of the product. <br /> <br /> Taking issue with one element of a setting, particularly one that involves the use of a real world slur, is not the same as advocating for anything resembling the \u2018sanitization\u2019 of a setting - it\u2019s advocating for making the setting more accessible and thus with greater potential for success and growth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-10T22:47:52-07:00","id":1407447,"title":"","content":"At the core of the issue discussed here, is this; No matter how dark the setting is, no matter what themes it has- the Setting should never turn around and tell you 'oh, you are not welcome here. We may use things from your culture here, but -you- as a person are not welcome to engage in this setting.' Especially in a game as socially aware as WtA.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-10T23:46:53-07:00","id":1407455,"title":"","content":"Look, you've all driven in decent points about the word metis, but is there a good way to reconcile an inoffensive solution with a toxic Garou culture? <br /> <br /> I had this funny (not funny) exhange in my head<br /> <br /> &quot;Ok, more than half the nation have agreed; we're not allowed to call you freaks metis anymore, it's insulting to a marginalized people some of us have ties to, and therefore a slur of the wyrm; What do you want to be called instead? Bastards, freaks, inbred, monstrosities, mistakes?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-11T00:46:05-07:00","id":1407459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1407286#post1407286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's what the books ask every Metis person that picks them up. That's why lots of us have spent decades advocating it get changed in some fashion. You're calling it an overblown non-issue because it doesn't make you put down the book and dismiss WtA in disgust. I actually lost players with Native backgrounds from an online Mage game just by mentioning I was a WtA fan in the late 90s.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is imo overly sensitive to borderline idiotic behaviour.<br /> <br /> But, as I employ my google fu it seems that the term is only used for the M\u00e9tis people today, and not an actively used term in the frensh language. Also, to relate it to the greek M\u00eatis seems wrong within the meaning of the word within the in-game universe - for while the Titaness M\u00eatis was kind of a double-edged sword situation for Zeus, the word also corresponds to 'wisdom' and that doesn't make sense as name for a breed.<br /> <br /> That said, if the 5th edition would simply use &quot;Mule&quot; as a term within the rules sections and descriptive texts and add an entry to the &quot;garou words&quot; section mentioning that the term &quot;Metis&quot; has fallen into disuse, especially with the rise of homids with political-correctness in mind.<br /> If W5 is to bridge a decade like V5 did, such a change would be believable, while not retconning the use of the word in the past.<br /> It still might not satisfy all Metis People, but unless someone emplys a TARDIS, it seems to me like a sensible approach. Then again, I'm not offended by the term.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-11T03:29:36-07:00","id":1407476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1407455#post1407455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Look, you've all driven in decent points about the word metis, but is there a good way to reconcile an inoffensive solution with a toxic Garou culture?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Plenty have been provided during the 8 pages of this. The thing is... most of us don't care about any sort of in-universe explanation for the change. Retconing it is fine. We don't need any sort of silly metaplot event that you seem to constantly harp on as a distraction from the issue.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1407459#post1407459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is imo overly sensitive to borderline idiotic behaviour.</div> </div> </div> </div>As you say, it's not a term that's being used that's insulting to you. It takes the most minimal application of empathy to understand why marginalized groups don't want to deal with casual racist language in their games and don't want to deal with gaming groups that accept such language in their gaming books.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...and that doesn't make sense as name for a breed. </div> </div> </div>That depends highly on what you think the point of having the Breed is (or at least was originally).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That said, if the 5th edition would simply use &quot;Mule&quot; as a term within the rules sections and descriptive texts and add an entry to the &quot;garou words&quot; section mentioning that the term &quot;Metis&quot; has fallen into disuse, especially with the rise of homids with political-correctness in mind. </div> </div> </div>It would be bullshit, as has been explained, repeatedly. It's not an in-universe problem that needs an in-universe solution. It's a problem with the writing of the game, and that's were it needs to be solved and acknowledged.<br /> <br /> Would it satisfy everyone? Of course not. But there's a lot you can do for goodwill by actually fixing and acknowledge why they needed fixed than worrying about retcons.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-11T07:32:30-07:00","id":1407503,"title":"","content":"This whole discussion is tiring because what I and Heavy Arms are saying is to make sure the PLAYERS will not feel attacked/offended about the material. Nothing about the in-universe treatment of metis. Just retiring one word and replacing it with maybe something from Latin like homid/lupus are?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-11T08:48:13-07:00","id":1407519,"title":"","content":"Instead of arguing ad nauseum, let's brainstorm new words.<ul><li>Mule, runt, wastrel, and maybe bastard are words Garou would use. Wiktionary tells me that <i>abhaic\u00edn</i> is Irish for 'runt', and lists <i>n\u00e1k\u02bceeshch\u0105\u0105\u02bc\u00ed</i> as the Navajo translation of 'runt'. It also gives lots of <a href=\"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bastard#Translations\" target=\"_blank\">translations for bastard</a>.</li> <li>Crinos is a word I could see the mules calling themselves to insist they deserve equality with homid and lupus, and to highlight their relation to all Garou, who all have a Crinos form.</li> <li>For Grondr, crinos works.</li> <li>Ratkin can't use runt, since that has a specific meaning for them already, and even mule might be a word only homids think to use. I like wastrel as a Ratkin term, <s>abecause theirs are sickly and less likey to survive the Birthing Plague</s>. Nvm, Wiktionary says 'wastrel' doesn't mean sickly.</li> <li>Kumo admire their in-between children, because they alone get to enjoy the fun of eating their mothers alive from the inside out. So... shinju ('pure') works for them. But does anyone know how to say &quot;devourer&quot; in Chinese or Japanese or Korean?</li> </ul><br /> <br /> What about the children of other Changing-Breeds? Does anyone know any African, South Asian, or Native American words that might be used by Bastet and Ajaba? Bastet admire their sterile children but for a less squick reason: because of the amazingly awesome Gifts they have (seriously, they are the most kickass in the Bastet Gifts list). I doubt Ajaba would call their mules 'runt' because for them, that would imply 'sickly animal that needs to be culled'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 08-11-2020, 12:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-11T08:50:03-07:00","id":1407520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1310339-metis-role-in-the-5th-edition?p=1407459#post1407459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is imo overly sensitive to borderline idiotic behaviour.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Don't talk to other posters this way.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/